1
00:02:26,486 --> 00:02:27,885
Osman..

2
00:02:28,326 --> 00:02:30,285
...look what your greed did to you.

3
00:02:30,646 --> 00:02:33,325
Look at your people's state.

4
00:02:40,486 --> 00:02:41,685
My Bey...

5
00:02:42,606 --> 00:02:45,605
Surely...

6
00:02:45,606 --> 00:02:48,525
...there will be a price for this oppression.

7
00:02:51,766 --> 00:02:52,805
Let her.

8
00:02:55,766 --> 00:02:59,165
Mother..

9
00:03:02,406 --> 00:03:04,845
We might be crying now...

10
00:03:04,926 --> 00:03:07,645
But we will not bow down, my Bey.

11
00:03:07,646 --> 00:03:10,445
Only this suits your people.

12
00:03:11,726 --> 00:03:14,565
As long as we have you...

13
00:03:14,566 --> 00:03:19,405
...this state will never collapse. Thank you.

14
00:03:21,526 --> 00:03:24,165
Walk! Come on walk!

15
00:03:41,246 --> 00:03:42,605
Altuga.

16
00:03:47,286 --> 00:03:49,725
Bring his Hatun and his children.

17
00:03:51,006 --> 00:03:54,885
Bring them, so they'll walk to death together.

18
00:03:55,686 --> 00:03:57,565
They ran away. Commander Ulugan.

19
00:04:00,406 --> 00:04:02,645
They ran away with a few people.

20
00:04:03,046 --> 00:04:05,345
Our nokers(Mongolian Soldiers) are after them.

21
00:04:05,345 --> 00:04:06,925
So they ran away, huh?

22
00:04:12,046 --> 00:04:18,845
Is there a hole in this world which can save
them from Mongols? Why are they even running?

23
00:04:21,086 --> 00:04:25,125
They are just growing the fire
of wrath that's waiting for them.

24
00:04:25,526 --> 00:04:27,885
This is your fate.

25
00:04:29,126 --> 00:04:32,645
You wrote this fate.

26
00:04:32,806 --> 00:04:39,125
I wish you could watch your
Hatun and your little dogs die.

27
00:04:40,046 --> 00:04:41,805
I wish, Osman.

28
00:04:42,806 --> 00:04:50,845
But apparently, death will take you before them.

29
00:04:52,486 --> 00:04:55,965
I will make your cause die.

30
00:04:55,966 --> 00:04:58,325
I will kill everyone from your family!

31
00:04:58,566 --> 00:05:03,485
Nothing will be left behind you, Osman.

32
00:05:03,486 --> 00:05:08,645
Even if you kill me, even
if you kill my children...

33
00:05:10,206 --> 00:05:12,645
...even if you leave no one behind...

34
00:05:14,926 --> 00:05:18,005
...the cause of Turks never die!

35
00:05:18,006 --> 00:05:19,845
Enough!

36
00:05:19,846 --> 00:05:23,365
Ghazi stop! What are you doing?

37
00:05:23,366 --> 00:05:25,645
-Ghazi!
-Stop...

38
00:05:25,646 --> 00:05:27,765
Stop, Cerkutay's dog, stop.

39
00:05:27,846 --> 00:05:34,605
Let go of me, you jackal -My valiant...

40
00:05:35,206 --> 00:05:39,843
The one you are trying to chain is
Osman Bey! He will make you pay for this!

41
00:05:39,855 --> 00:05:41,405
My valiant...

42
00:05:41,926 --> 00:05:43,325
Nokers(Mongolian Soldiers).

43
00:05:43,406 --> 00:05:45,465
Take this one to the tent.

44
00:05:46,446 --> 00:05:49,085
Don't touch me!
-Don't worry...

45
00:05:49,086 --> 00:05:50,245
My Bey...

46
00:05:50,246 --> 00:05:52,005
Don't worry.

47
00:05:56,126 --> 00:05:57,485
Do you see?

48
00:05:58,726 --> 00:06:00,045
A child..

49
00:06:00,366 --> 00:06:03,045
...a Hatun, a man...

50
00:06:03,846 --> 00:06:07,805
There is always someone who
will protect the cause of Turks.

51
00:06:08,326 --> 00:06:10,845
No one can disrupt our unity.

52
00:06:11,446 --> 00:06:12,925
We will see Osman.

53
00:06:14,046 --> 00:06:15,445
We will see.

54
00:06:16,086 --> 00:06:20,565
We will see the situation of people...

55
00:06:21,086 --> 00:06:23,525
...while their Bey is dying in my hands.

56
00:06:26,446 --> 00:06:28,205
Prepare the setup.

57
00:06:29,366 --> 00:06:32,365
Osman will be the target of my arrows.

58
00:06:34,526 --> 00:06:36,885
My Bey!

59
00:06:36,886 --> 00:06:38,965
My Bey, don't!

60
00:06:38,966 --> 00:06:39,885
My Bey!

61
00:06:43,566 --> 00:06:47,965
-My Bey, don't!
-Don't worry.

62
00:06:48,206 --> 00:06:51,405
Don't worry...

63
00:07:14,286 --> 00:07:15,765
Come on! Come on!

64
00:07:20,766 --> 00:07:22,165
We are safe for now.

65
00:07:22,166 --> 00:07:25,845
Have some rest. -Come on.

66
00:07:25,846 --> 00:07:28,805
Orhan..

67
00:07:30,606 --> 00:07:32,125
Sit down.

68
00:07:36,686 --> 00:07:41,685
Don't be afraid.
Don't be afraid.

69
00:07:41,686 --> 00:07:42,965
Help.

70
00:07:42,966 --> 00:07:46,485
Mother... Where is my father?

71
00:07:50,446 --> 00:07:52,605
We learned that he was in Sogut.

72
00:07:53,406 --> 00:07:56,285
We cannot leave my father in those dogs' hands.

73
00:07:56,366 --> 00:07:59,485
We won't. Orhan, Alaeddin.

74
00:07:59,486 --> 00:08:02,125
Orhan, treat his wounds, my son.
-Brother...

75
00:08:02,126 --> 00:08:04,845
Stop, Alaeddin. Wait.

76
00:08:05,406 --> 00:08:06,445
Mother..

77
00:08:06,606 --> 00:08:08,845
My wounds are not important.

78
00:08:08,926 --> 00:08:10,725
My father is.

79
00:08:11,126 --> 00:08:14,525
We will not leave my father
in those dastard dogs' hands.

80
00:08:15,526 --> 00:08:16,765
My Shahzade...

81
00:08:17,206 --> 00:08:18,685
Wear this...

82
00:08:22,646 --> 00:08:27,765
Thank you Samil. -You are not alright...

83
00:08:27,846 --> 00:08:29,725
You are covered in bruises.

84
00:08:29,966 --> 00:08:35,365
I am alright, my Holofira. I
am alright, don't worry. I am...

85
00:08:37,405 --> 00:08:39,365
Ghazi!

86
00:08:43,206 --> 00:08:46,365
Ghazi is not here, Cerkutay!

87
00:08:46,366 --> 00:08:49,285
Ghazi is not here, Cerkutay!
-Ghazi..

88
00:08:49,646 --> 00:08:50,685
Ghazi?

89
00:08:54,046 --> 00:08:55,645
Ghazi?

90
00:08:55,646 --> 00:08:57,325
Ghazi!

91
00:08:57,686 --> 00:08:58,765
Ghazi!

92
00:08:59,446 --> 00:09:02,285
Have you seen Ghazi? Ghazi!

93
00:09:03,646 --> 00:09:05,205
He is not here!

94
00:09:05,206 --> 00:09:07,725
Ghazi! Where is Ghazi!

95
00:09:07,966 --> 00:09:10,845
Ulgen! Ulgen, when was
the last time you saw him?

96
00:09:10,966 --> 00:09:13,045
Meryem... He was with Meryem.

97
00:09:13,686 --> 00:09:14,885
Meryem?

98
00:09:15,406 --> 00:09:17,365
Meryem, mother! Meryem is not here!

99
00:09:17,366 --> 00:09:19,165
Did they get caught?

100
00:09:20,126 --> 00:09:22,325
They were right behind us!

101
00:09:22,686 --> 00:09:24,685
Ghazi is not here!
Ghazi is not here!

102
00:09:24,686 --> 00:09:27,325
Ghazi is not here!

103
00:09:27,326 --> 00:09:30,045
Ghazi!

104
00:09:30,046 --> 00:09:34,565
Turhan Alp! Ghazi is not here!
-Stop... Stop!

105
00:09:34,606 --> 00:09:38,085
Brother, those dogs will kill
you once you arrive in the tribe.

106
00:09:38,086 --> 00:09:41,365
You are walking to fire, brother. Don't!
-I cannot stop, brother!

107
00:09:41,366 --> 00:09:44,285
Ghazi is in the hands of
Mongols! How can I stop?!

108
00:09:44,446 --> 00:09:47,085
Brother! -Cerkutay, stop!

109
00:09:47,606 --> 00:09:49,565
Ghazi is strong and brave.

110
00:09:49,686 --> 00:09:55,125
Besides, that dog named
Altuga would never kill Ghazi.

111
00:09:55,126 --> 00:09:57,445
-I have to go!
-We will find him!

112
00:09:57,806 --> 00:10:00,245
We will find him Cerkutay, we will!
-Brother...

113
00:10:00,246 --> 00:10:03,685
We will find him, don't worry!
-I cannot wait here, my Shahzade!

114
00:10:03,766 --> 00:10:07,645
They will take him from me!
They will take him from me!

115
00:10:07,646 --> 00:10:10,925
No one will take him! No one!

116
00:10:11,206 --> 00:10:13,205
Cerkutay! Cerkutay!

117
00:10:13,206 --> 00:10:14,845
We will not let this happen.

118
00:10:14,846 --> 00:10:18,085
We will save him from there safe
and sound, like our other people.

119
00:10:18,086 --> 00:10:20,805
But not now, we have to act wisely now!

120
00:10:25,046 --> 00:10:27,605
Bala Hatun! Bala Hatun!

121
00:10:32,526 --> 00:10:35,205
The dastards took Osman Bey to the tribe.

122
00:10:39,206 --> 00:10:42,245
We can see the tribe from the hilltop. Let's go.

123
00:10:42,286 --> 00:10:44,645
Alright. Fatma, Ulgen.

124
00:10:45,086 --> 00:10:48,125
You and Alp take people
to the tents behind Karadin.

125
00:10:48,246 --> 00:10:52,085
It was evacuated before.
Nobody would know. Come on.

126
00:10:52,286 --> 00:10:55,325
Come on, Ulgen. Let's go.

127
00:10:55,406 --> 00:10:57,805
-Let's go to the hilltop.
-Come on.

128
00:10:57,806 --> 00:11:01,005
-We'll save him. Let's go.
-Come on, come on.

129
00:11:01,046 --> 00:11:02,685
Come on.

130
00:11:02,806 --> 00:11:04,925
Impertinent Bey of Kayi.

131
00:11:05,526 --> 00:11:07,925
Your sons who ran away...

132
00:11:08,966 --> 00:11:10,885
While I kill them.

133
00:11:11,726 --> 00:11:14,845
...I won't be as merciful as I'm to you.

134
00:11:18,726 --> 00:11:20,045
Come on.

135
00:11:21,646 --> 00:11:23,125
Untie my hands.

136
00:11:23,646 --> 00:11:24,645
Come on.

137
00:11:24,886 --> 00:11:26,685
Grab your sword and fight me.

138
00:11:26,926 --> 00:11:29,006
Fight me if you have courage.

139
00:11:30,006 --> 00:11:34,285
So I can show you what the frontiers are.

140
00:11:35,286 --> 00:11:39,005
So I can return your cruelty.

141
00:11:40,126 --> 00:11:40,885
No.

142
00:11:42,566 --> 00:11:49,125
Killing you like a soldier would a gift for you.

143
00:11:50,126 --> 00:11:52,485
You will fall in weakness.

144
00:11:55,646 --> 00:11:58,125
Yusuf, they'll kill Osman Bey.

145
00:11:58,486 --> 00:12:00,645
They'll murder him vilely.

146
00:12:00,886 --> 00:12:03,965
Dastards! Dogs!

147
00:12:04,486 --> 00:12:07,205
If my Bey is killed.

148
00:12:07,326 --> 00:12:11,245
...then Kayi will make your lives miserable!

149
00:12:11,366 --> 00:12:14,645
With Allah's will, they will! Dastards!

150
00:12:14,926 --> 00:12:17,525
Dastards! Dastards!

151
00:12:17,606 --> 00:12:19,565
Release our Bey, tyrants!

152
00:12:19,686 --> 00:12:21,925
You've tortured enough!

153
00:12:22,926 --> 00:12:27,845
You and your people, even in this situation.

154
00:12:28,006 --> 00:12:31,445
...never lose your courage.

155
00:12:31,686 --> 00:12:35,925
This courage will destroy...

156
00:12:36,486 --> 00:12:40,405
...you and all of your
people who rise with cruelty!

157
00:12:43,886 --> 00:12:46,845
Where did they take Ghazi, Meryem?

158
00:12:47,086 --> 00:12:49,885
They won't harm Ghazi, will they?

159
00:12:51,166 --> 00:12:54,485
-They won't hurt him.
-Don't worry, Ayse.

160
00:12:55,126 --> 00:12:56,765
He will be fine.

161
00:12:57,606 --> 00:13:00,285
My father must have left with Bala Hatun.

162
00:13:00,726 --> 00:13:04,045
But I know... He's going to save us.

163
00:13:23,166 --> 00:13:28,085
Look, Osman. The last guests
you'll host in your tribe are coming.

164
00:13:38,326 --> 00:13:40,365
Vile dogs!

165
00:13:41,486 --> 00:13:44,285
You didn't only enter the wolf's tent...

166
00:13:45,566 --> 00:13:48,045
...but also took your jackals with you, huh?

167
00:13:52,126 --> 00:13:56,845
You always take the smell
of the feast and arrive in time!

168
00:13:58,406 --> 00:14:00,845
You execute the bey of Kayi..

169
00:14:02,526 --> 00:14:05,245
...and we miss the show?

170
00:14:06,286 --> 00:14:08,005
Not in this world.

171
00:14:08,606 --> 00:14:10,845
Vile dog!

172
00:14:12,566 --> 00:14:14,205
Well..

173
00:14:15,006 --> 00:14:15,885
Where is Bala?

174
00:14:16,566 --> 00:14:18,485
She will be the next.

175
00:14:22,326 --> 00:14:24,845
As long as I keep breathing,

176
00:14:25,766 --> 00:14:28,125
...you will be the next ones to die.

177
00:14:34,126 --> 00:14:35,925
You will die too.

178
00:14:36,046 --> 00:14:37,485
Inglorious Sofia!

179
00:14:37,886 --> 00:14:40,125
You'll die too! Don't worry!

180
00:14:41,486 --> 00:14:42,685
Osman.

181
00:14:43,566 --> 00:14:45,565
Before I kill you

182
00:14:46,246 --> 00:14:48,725
...there is something I want to show you.

183
00:14:50,606 --> 00:14:52,125
Bring him.

184
00:15:07,166 --> 00:15:09,165
Vile dastards!

185
00:15:10,606 --> 00:15:13,205
-Lukas...
You'll see.

186
00:15:13,686 --> 00:15:15,605
We will make you pay.

187
00:15:37,086 --> 00:15:38,685
Ilbay.

188
00:15:46,286 --> 00:15:48,685
What are you doing there?

189
00:15:52,606 --> 00:15:54,005
Not only Ilbay.

190
00:15:56,726 --> 00:15:59,165
You should know the man on your chair.

191
00:16:02,246 --> 00:16:04,245
The new Bey of Kayi.

192
00:16:05,006 --> 00:16:08,885
Ilbay Bey, grandson of Sungur Tegin.

193
00:16:13,086 --> 00:16:15,365
What?

194
00:16:23,126 --> 00:16:24,885
Leave me.

195
00:16:26,766 --> 00:16:28,605
Leave me.

196
00:16:38,086 --> 00:16:43,125
My... My uncle...

197
00:16:45,286 --> 00:16:49,245
...Sungur Tegin's grandson, huh?

198
00:16:49,966 --> 00:16:51,805
You heard right, Osman.

199
00:16:52,806 --> 00:16:57,165
I'm the grandson of Sungur Tegin...

200
00:16:57,886 --> 00:17:00,845
...who made great efforts
for the future of Turks.

201
00:17:17,326 --> 00:17:19,204
And you, Begum Hatun?

202
00:17:19,886 --> 00:17:22,405
-I am...
Begum Hatun...

203
00:17:26,046 --> 00:17:28,085
...is my wife-to-be.

204
00:17:38,006 --> 00:17:39,885
Don't look at me like that, Osman.

205
00:17:40,246 --> 00:17:42,085
This is divine justice.

206
00:17:43,166 --> 00:17:47,245
This is the day when the
right will regain his rights.

207
00:17:49,766 --> 00:17:51,725
Is that...

208
00:17:55,246 --> 00:18:02,045
Is that why you stayed with me for so long?

209
00:18:07,566 --> 00:18:10,565
Did you think this was your right?

210
00:18:12,086 --> 00:18:14,685
You were dreaming of this throne, huh?

211
00:18:16,166 --> 00:18:17,645
Is that why...

212
00:18:17,806 --> 00:18:22,205
...you worked with these
dogs and came close to me?

213
00:18:24,406 --> 00:18:27,405
I don't want anything else
but what is mine, Osman.

214
00:18:27,926 --> 00:18:30,405
My grandfather Sungur Tegin Bey...

215
00:18:30,606 --> 00:18:35,365
...was a warrior who sacrificed
his title and life for Kayi.

216
00:18:36,206 --> 00:18:39,725
-This chair has always been my right!
-Shut up!

217
00:18:52,926 --> 00:18:55,165
You see, Lukas?

218
00:18:55,926 --> 00:19:00,685
I told you Ilbay was more than he looked.

219
00:19:01,486 --> 00:19:07,165
A dagger that Osman trusted so
much and that stuck into his heart.

220
00:19:08,966 --> 00:19:11,245
You dastard.

221
00:19:12,806 --> 00:19:14,285
You..

222
00:19:15,486 --> 00:19:20,725
You let all these dogs in the state tent...

223
00:19:21,206 --> 00:19:24,325
...and you say you are Kayi

224
00:19:25,086 --> 00:19:28,005
While all our people are tortured outside!

225
00:19:29,286 --> 00:19:31,325
Don't you have any honor?

226
00:19:31,926 --> 00:19:36,285
Don't you have any dignity at all?

227
00:19:36,646 --> 00:19:38,485
Know your...

228
00:19:49,446 --> 00:19:51,605
All these people here...

229
00:19:52,406 --> 00:19:56,805
...are the new masters and allies of Kayi.

230
00:19:58,286 --> 00:20:01,205
The new head of Kayi is Ilbay.

231
00:20:02,046 --> 00:20:05,005
Kayi belongs to Mongolians now.

232
00:20:05,966 --> 00:20:12,005
Your alps, people and everyone else...

233
00:20:13,446 --> 00:20:15,605
...are servants of Mongolians now.

234
00:20:28,526 --> 00:20:32,965
Turks can never be dominated.

235
00:20:33,126 --> 00:20:38,525
They will! It will be whatever I say!

236
00:20:42,886 --> 00:20:45,285
Sofia and Lukas are...

237
00:20:46,126 --> 00:20:49,205
...Kayi's allies from now on.

238
00:21:08,686 --> 00:21:13,605
Your cryings of conquest have brought nothing
but blood and death in these lands, Osman.

239
00:21:13,606 --> 00:21:17,005
I will do just the opposite and
take a good care of my people.

240
00:21:17,566 --> 00:21:19,485
I will help this glorious state...

241
00:21:19,766 --> 00:21:22,485
...reach peace and rest.

242
00:21:22,966 --> 00:21:28,165
What you will reach will
be only captivity and defeat.

243
00:21:29,646 --> 00:21:32,525
You'll never be worthy of...

244
00:21:33,206 --> 00:21:37,245
...my uncle Sungur Tegin or Kayi.

245
00:21:55,006 --> 00:21:59,205
-I won't leave you to them, Osman.
-Here they are!

246
00:22:01,806 --> 00:22:04,845
-Behind the trees!
-Come here.

247
00:22:15,566 --> 00:22:16,734
They're approaching.

248
00:22:16,746 --> 00:22:19,725
We'll strike them like
lightnings with our swords!

249
00:22:19,766 --> 00:22:22,285
Boran Bey, shoot your arrows!

250
00:22:22,406 --> 00:22:25,885
Kill those dogs running to their death!

251
00:22:28,726 --> 00:22:31,125
-Are you alright?
-I'm good.

252
00:22:33,926 --> 00:22:36,805
Orhan, you aren't well.

253
00:22:39,446 --> 00:22:44,965
Look, your wound hurts my heart. You stay back.

254
00:22:45,086 --> 00:22:48,045
-We can handle this.
-I'm good, Holofira.

255
00:22:48,406 --> 00:22:52,325
Before my father is saved
from those Mongolian dogs,

256
00:22:52,806 --> 00:22:56,325
...my wound is my fellow.

257
00:22:56,766 --> 00:22:58,045
Orhan..

258
00:23:00,086 --> 00:23:02,365
-I am... Holofira.

259
00:23:06,006 --> 00:23:08,725
Gonca, you stay with Holofira.

260
00:23:08,846 --> 00:23:12,445
-She's carrying a baby.
-I'll look after them. Don't worry.

261
00:23:13,166 --> 00:23:17,125
-Come on, come on.
-Allah is the greatest!

262
00:23:25,486 --> 00:23:27,885
-Come on!
-Come on.

263
00:23:27,966 --> 00:23:29,725
Come on.

264
00:24:36,526 --> 00:24:40,245
Why do you love cruel Osman so much?

265
00:24:57,246 --> 00:24:59,005
Let our Bey go!

266
00:24:59,006 --> 00:25:03,885
You should all learn a lesson
from the things you will see here.

267
00:25:07,086 --> 00:25:13,445
See what Mongols do to those who oppose
and what they offer to those who obey.

268
00:25:17,446 --> 00:25:24,645
While Osman is going to
death, greet the new Bey of Kayi.

269
00:25:27,166 --> 00:25:28,685
New Kayi Bey?

270
00:25:32,806 --> 00:25:38,485
New Kayi Bey is Sungur
Tekin's grandson Ilbay Bey!

271
00:25:58,686 --> 00:26:01,365
Ilbay? Traitor Ilbay!

272
00:26:26,846 --> 00:26:27,885
Father..

273
00:26:30,526 --> 00:26:32,405
Is Ilbay a Kayi?

274
00:26:34,926 --> 00:26:37,245
What did you do, father?

275
00:26:40,526 --> 00:26:42,845
Begum Hatun..

276
00:26:43,406 --> 00:26:49,445
Sister... Sister, what are you trying to do?
-Traitor...

277
00:27:09,286 --> 00:27:11,885
Dastards..

278
00:27:18,726 --> 00:27:19,885
Dastards..

279
00:28:44,846 --> 00:28:47,725
Before we kill one of these
dogs, the others come!

280
00:28:48,686 --> 00:28:54,565
Ulugan dog sent his dogs everywhere!

281
00:29:03,086 --> 00:29:05,725
We will not stop even if
there is shahada in the end!

282
00:29:22,406 --> 00:29:24,765
Dastard dog!

283
00:29:24,766 --> 00:29:28,485
Now, your people who are begging to save you...

284
00:29:28,646 --> 00:29:34,085
...will soon obey Mongols and
remember you as a traitor, Osman.

285
00:29:47,206 --> 00:29:53,925
Oghuz' blessed lineage never
bows down to you or dogs like you.

286
00:29:54,726 --> 00:30:00,685
Those like you can only find
peace by dying on these lands.

287
00:30:02,006 --> 00:30:06,125
I know how to turn that
blessed people into sheep.

288
00:30:06,766 --> 00:30:08,085
Nokers(Mongolian Soldiers).

289
00:30:08,646 --> 00:30:12,125
Tie Osman Bey up. Tie him up tightly.

290
00:31:06,646 --> 00:31:08,125
Come on!

291
00:31:19,286 --> 00:31:21,805
We will now understand what these dogs want!

292
00:31:21,806 --> 00:31:26,005
Come on, to the hill! Come on!
-Come on!

293
00:31:26,006 --> 00:31:28,085
Come on!

294
00:31:32,246 --> 00:31:38,125
See the end of the one who
stood against the Mongols.

295
00:31:38,806 --> 00:31:42,405
This will be a lesson to everyone.

296
00:31:49,486 --> 00:31:51,805
O, my suffering people...

297
00:31:51,806 --> 00:31:54,725
...who resists every hardship.

298
00:31:55,646 --> 00:31:58,605
Why are we still letting him speak?
-Let him speak...

299
00:31:58,606 --> 00:32:01,005
It's his last words anyway.

300
00:32:02,846 --> 00:32:05,365
I will never forgive you, father.

301
00:32:07,526 --> 00:32:09,125
Lift your head.

302
00:32:10,726 --> 00:32:12,525
Lift your head

303
00:32:14,926 --> 00:32:17,005
We will always stand tall!

304
00:32:18,486 --> 00:32:20,645
Even if they shed our blood...

305
00:32:21,686 --> 00:32:23,445
...even if they bury our bodies...

306
00:32:24,606 --> 00:32:26,965
...they will never gain a victory.

307
00:32:28,566 --> 00:32:30,045
You will never...

308
00:32:30,246 --> 00:32:32,685
...cry after me!

309
00:32:35,926 --> 00:32:38,285
You will not lose your hope!

310
00:32:38,926 --> 00:32:40,485
Even if I die...

311
00:32:40,806 --> 00:32:47,125
You will forever follow and
protect my ever-lasting da'wah.

312
00:32:49,406 --> 00:33:00,885
Now those who put us into this
situation must know, even if I die...

313
00:33:02,766 --> 00:33:07,965
...those who will come after me
will never bow down to captivity!

314
00:33:08,446 --> 00:33:13,645
Who can make Turks who are in
love with The Righteous and freedom kneel?

315
00:33:16,886 --> 00:33:19,245
You are at the end of the way, Osman.

316
00:33:19,246 --> 00:33:22,245
Even when he is at the
end, he is still ambitious.

317
00:33:32,206 --> 00:33:35,925
I will rip your heart out.

318
00:33:42,046 --> 00:33:46,445
I bear witness that there is none
worthy of worship except Allah...

319
00:33:46,446 --> 00:33:51,045
...and I bear witness that Muhammad(PBUH)
is His servant and Messenger.

320
00:34:35,166 --> 00:34:38,165
Who dares to do that? Who?!

321
00:34:38,166 --> 00:34:42,205
Who is trying to save
Osman's life? Show yourself!

322
00:35:00,086 --> 00:35:01,485
Thanks to Allah..

323
00:35:02,086 --> 00:35:03,485
Who is that?

324
00:35:03,966 --> 00:35:05,085
It's a messenger.

325
00:35:05,086 --> 00:35:08,885
Mongol messenger.

326
00:35:14,646 --> 00:35:16,485
It's Olcaytu Khan...

327
00:35:18,046 --> 00:35:20,005
...who saved Osman's life.

328
00:35:30,486 --> 00:35:32,445
Olcaytu Khan, huh?

329
00:35:33,126 --> 00:35:34,525
Why did our Khan..

330
00:35:35,006 --> 00:35:37,845
...stop Osman's execution?

331
00:35:37,846 --> 00:35:41,245
Only our Khan knows that. He ordered...

332
00:35:41,326 --> 00:35:44,565
...Osman to be taken to Tabriz immediately.

333
00:35:47,366 --> 00:35:49,125
How is this possible, Ulugan?

334
00:35:51,526 --> 00:35:55,405
It is possible if Olcaytu Khan orders so.

335
00:35:59,726 --> 00:36:03,645
Altuga, prepare the caged cart.

336
00:36:03,886 --> 00:36:06,005
You will take him there.

337
00:36:08,046 --> 00:36:10,965
Nokers(Mongolian Soldiers),
you heard the commander...

338
00:36:13,486 --> 00:36:15,885
My Allah..

339
00:36:19,086 --> 00:36:21,085
You are the Greatest.

340
00:36:25,806 --> 00:36:27,165
Now...

341
00:36:27,566 --> 00:36:30,565
...since this heart is
still beating in this body...

342
00:36:32,806 --> 00:36:35,725
...you are the ones who should be afraid.

343
00:36:38,606 --> 00:36:41,765
Do not forget who you are going to see, Osman.

344
00:36:43,166 --> 00:36:44,405
If there is someone..

345
00:36:45,246 --> 00:36:47,805
...who needs to be afraid, that's you.

346
00:36:57,686 --> 00:37:01,405
They are bringing the caged
cart. They will go somewhere.

347
00:37:01,806 --> 00:37:03,885
We know where they will take him.

348
00:37:04,406 --> 00:37:06,365
Either to the Mongol palace...

349
00:37:06,966 --> 00:37:09,645
...or the Mongol lands.

350
00:37:10,206 --> 00:37:11,885
You are right, brother.

351
00:37:13,126 --> 00:37:14,765
Only Olcaytu...

352
00:37:15,166 --> 00:37:17,005
...can stop Ulugan.

353
00:37:20,686 --> 00:37:25,005
My Osman Bey! My Osman Bey!

354
00:37:29,886 --> 00:37:32,725
Don't cry...

355
00:37:36,806 --> 00:37:38,805
Don't cry...

356
00:37:38,806 --> 00:37:41,365
My father betrayed you, my Osman Bey.

357
00:37:41,566 --> 00:37:45,925
He betrayed your lineage. -No...

358
00:37:47,606 --> 00:37:51,445
As long as we have brave warriors like you...

359
00:37:54,166 --> 00:37:56,965
...traitors among us won't be able to upset us.

360
00:38:00,646 --> 00:38:01,725
Ayse...

361
00:38:06,846 --> 00:38:10,125
Ayse. Come on. Go.

362
00:38:11,806 --> 00:38:13,885
My daughter, come here. -Don't touch me.

363
00:38:13,886 --> 00:38:15,685
Put him in the cart.

364
00:38:31,246 --> 00:38:34,685
My Allah helped us. Our Bey is alive.

365
00:38:34,766 --> 00:38:37,005
Now we need to save him.

366
00:38:37,686 --> 00:38:39,565
This is our duty.

367
00:38:40,086 --> 00:38:42,285
But there are too many of them.

368
00:38:42,526 --> 00:38:44,365
Nokers(Mongolian Soldiers)
are forming a line.

369
00:38:44,886 --> 00:38:49,045
When they leave the tribe, we
can trap them in the narrow valley.

370
00:38:49,126 --> 00:38:51,165
Then we will have the advantage.

371
00:38:51,766 --> 00:38:53,965
We will open the door of that cage.

372
00:38:54,926 --> 00:38:59,205
No matter what it costs, we
will open the door of that cage.

373
00:38:59,406 --> 00:39:01,085
We cannot go there on foot.

374
00:39:01,286 --> 00:39:02,765
We need horses.

375
00:39:03,246 --> 00:39:04,645
You are right.

376
00:39:05,206 --> 00:39:07,165
Turhan. Alps.

377
00:39:07,166 --> 00:39:10,205
Find horses immediately.
-As you order.

378
00:39:12,446 --> 00:39:14,565
Today, everything is for our state.

379
00:39:15,526 --> 00:39:18,725
Osman Bey's struggle is our struggle.

380
00:39:18,846 --> 00:39:23,845
May Allah help us.
-Aameen. -Aameen.

381
00:39:23,846 --> 00:39:26,365
Come on, get ready.

382
00:39:27,846 --> 00:39:31,525
Altuga, convey my respects to our Khan.

383
00:39:43,686 --> 00:39:48,805
Set our Bey free!

384
00:39:48,806 --> 00:39:53,725
Traitors! -Don't touch me!

385
00:39:58,526 --> 00:40:00,885
Even if it is Olcaytu Khan's order,

386
00:40:02,486 --> 00:40:05,885
...it's not right to leave Osman
alive, Commander Ulugan.

387
00:40:07,446 --> 00:40:09,845
Are you afraid of his power...

388
00:40:11,046 --> 00:40:13,925
...as long as he keeps breathing?

389
00:40:14,326 --> 00:40:15,325
Don't be.

390
00:40:15,406 --> 00:40:20,525
We will make only our own power rule you.

391
00:40:25,166 --> 00:40:27,445
Ilbay is right, Ulugan.

392
00:40:27,726 --> 00:40:31,165
You should have killed
Osman while you had a chance.

393
00:40:31,406 --> 00:40:35,765
Bala, Orhan... They're all missing.
They will never stop following Osman.

394
00:40:36,126 --> 00:40:38,085
That's what I want, hatun.

395
00:40:38,526 --> 00:40:41,685
Let them attempt to reach Osman.

396
00:40:42,806 --> 00:40:45,045
They will be my preys.

397
00:40:59,206 --> 00:41:00,605
Sister.

398
00:41:00,966 --> 00:41:02,805
What have you done?

399
00:41:03,126 --> 00:41:05,685
How could you betray Osman Bey, sister?

400
00:41:05,966 --> 00:41:08,085
We'll talk, brother.

401
00:41:09,646 --> 00:41:12,605
Release Yusuf Bey. He's
Ilbay Bey's brother-in-law.

402
00:41:12,966 --> 00:41:15,645
What are you talking about, sister?

403
00:41:16,006 --> 00:41:19,085
I already knew your nature, Begum Hatun!

404
00:41:21,086 --> 00:41:22,685
You are a traitor!

405
00:41:23,046 --> 00:41:24,645
Traitor.

406
00:41:28,926 --> 00:41:30,725
What have you done, sister?

407
00:41:31,286 --> 00:41:32,445
What have you done?

408
00:42:08,246 --> 00:42:13,405
You didn't die but you will
taste even much worse in Tabriz.

409
00:42:23,006 --> 00:42:26,045
You'll never be able to come back to your tribe.

410
00:43:01,326 --> 00:43:03,485
My bird.

411
00:43:06,526 --> 00:43:09,045
Thank God, you're fine.

412
00:43:10,446 --> 00:43:12,005
My aunt.

413
00:43:12,446 --> 00:43:15,405
I missed you so much.
-Look.

414
00:43:15,646 --> 00:43:19,325
Thanks to you, Osman's reign is over.

415
00:43:19,966 --> 00:43:24,805
Kayi people are just a broken herd now.

416
00:43:25,766 --> 00:43:27,885
Aunt...

417
00:43:30,126 --> 00:43:32,765
Mongolians killed too many people.

418
00:43:33,566 --> 00:43:36,445
They left many orphans behind.

419
00:43:37,606 --> 00:43:41,045
Osman is a bad man. That's right.

420
00:43:42,566 --> 00:43:45,365
But he's a good leader, aunt.

421
00:43:47,566 --> 00:43:50,685
Are you defending Osman, Poena?

422
00:43:52,606 --> 00:43:56,565
The man who slaughtered
your parents mercilessly.

423
00:43:57,606 --> 00:44:02,085
The man who left you alone
among the dead bodies.

424
00:44:06,246 --> 00:44:08,685
If your parents heard this.

425
00:44:09,286 --> 00:44:12,045
..they would die once again due to sorrow.

426
00:44:12,926 --> 00:44:14,525
Osman..

427
00:44:15,406 --> 00:44:19,165
...tortured them to death.

428
00:44:25,366 --> 00:44:27,445
I'm sorry, aunt.

429
00:44:29,206 --> 00:44:33,285
They acted so sincerely to me...

430
00:44:34,326 --> 00:44:40,325
Osman and Bala acted warmly to you, didn't they?

431
00:44:43,486 --> 00:44:47,525
You thought they cared for you.

432
00:44:48,966 --> 00:44:50,805
Well..

433
00:44:51,126 --> 00:44:53,445
This is their biggest weapon.

434
00:44:56,086 --> 00:44:57,765
And you...

435
00:44:58,606 --> 00:45:01,645
...got deceived by their
fake faces, my little bird.

436
00:45:03,566 --> 00:45:07,565
They never cared for you. They just pitied.

437
00:45:09,046 --> 00:45:11,045
When I got poisoned,

438
00:45:11,606 --> 00:45:17,125
...Osman and Bala looked
after me as if I were their family.

439
00:45:18,926 --> 00:45:25,605
Osman said he would protect me, aunt.

440
00:45:26,486 --> 00:45:28,965
Well, Poena...

441
00:45:29,846 --> 00:45:32,485
Their words are poisonous.

442
00:45:32,886 --> 00:45:37,085
They put you in this situation. Look.

443
00:45:38,886 --> 00:45:41,125
All alone.

444
00:45:45,486 --> 00:45:47,805
A lonely kid.

445
00:46:01,286 --> 00:46:03,485
Remember your hatred.

446
00:46:04,366 --> 00:46:06,805
Remember your parents.

447
00:46:18,446 --> 00:46:21,085
Crying doesn't suit you at all.

448
00:46:24,886 --> 00:46:26,965
You're right, aunt.

449
00:46:27,326 --> 00:46:28,685
You're right.

450
00:46:29,686 --> 00:46:34,005
I was deceived by their tricks.

451
00:46:35,166 --> 00:46:37,125
Today is the vengeance day.

452
00:46:38,846 --> 00:46:41,485
Go after Osman and kill him.

453
00:46:42,606 --> 00:46:46,365
Osman has to die for your
parents to rest in peace.

454
00:46:47,126 --> 00:46:49,405
You have my word.

455
00:46:50,526 --> 00:46:54,365
I promise I will kill you aunt.

456
00:46:56,406 --> 00:46:58,965
I'm sure you will succeed.

457
00:47:02,046 --> 00:47:06,885
Aunt, I want Osman's horse.

458
00:47:07,446 --> 00:47:09,525
I will ride on him.

459
00:47:11,206 --> 00:47:13,685
Can you control him?

460
00:47:25,566 --> 00:47:29,365
Mongolians always use this route.

461
00:47:30,646 --> 00:47:33,755
And their nokers(Mongolian Soldiers)
take positions in these spots.

462
00:47:34,646 --> 00:47:37,605
You say they will go through
this, right, my Shahzade?

463
00:47:43,526 --> 00:47:46,525
We need to catch up before
they get out of our borders.

464
00:47:47,486 --> 00:47:51,485
Then we need to use the short cut quickly...

465
00:47:52,046 --> 00:47:54,405
...and ambush them on the way.

466
00:47:54,406 --> 00:47:57,765
Before they get out of borders,
we will take Osman Bey back.

467
00:47:57,806 --> 00:47:59,085
God willing.

468
00:48:00,846 --> 00:48:02,605
May Allah help us all.

469
00:48:02,606 --> 00:48:05,285
-Aameen.
-Aameen.

470
00:48:16,606 --> 00:48:18,205
Here we go!

471
00:48:33,166 --> 00:48:34,965
Come on

472
00:49:00,406 --> 00:49:01,565
What's going on here?

473
00:49:01,606 --> 00:49:03,965
Bala Hatun's horse is bad tempered.

474
00:49:04,046 --> 00:49:05,925
It's trying to run off.

475
00:49:17,006 --> 00:49:20,725
Alaca, do you want to go to Bala?

476
00:49:22,206 --> 00:49:24,045
Bala just abandoned you, though.

477
00:49:27,966 --> 00:49:29,365
Don't be upset.

478
00:49:29,806 --> 00:49:31,845
You will be my horse, alright?

479
00:49:33,966 --> 00:49:36,365
Don't try in vain.

480
00:49:38,366 --> 00:49:40,485
She lets nobody else but Bala.

481
00:49:41,286 --> 00:49:42,685
She's loyal to her owner.

482
00:49:43,126 --> 00:49:45,965
I will cut off..

483
00:49:47,006 --> 00:49:49,645
...people and this horse's loyalty to Bala.

484
00:49:50,166 --> 00:49:53,885
They will even forget Bala's name.

485
00:49:58,206 --> 00:49:59,805
And you?

486
00:50:02,006 --> 00:50:04,365
Can you take Osman's place?

487
00:50:18,566 --> 00:50:22,125
I'm not impatient like you.
I'm waiting for my time.

488
00:50:23,326 --> 00:50:25,605
Osman will vanish when it's time.

489
00:50:26,646 --> 00:50:28,525
And my reign will begin.

490
00:50:30,566 --> 00:50:34,605
I will be such a bey to them that
they won't even remember Osman.

491
00:50:35,766 --> 00:50:37,885
Osman is alive, though.

492
00:50:38,446 --> 00:50:39,925
What if he comes back?

493
00:50:40,326 --> 00:50:42,765
What if he makes you pay for what you did?

494
00:50:43,766 --> 00:50:45,005
What?

495
00:50:45,526 --> 00:50:47,125
Are you afraid?

496
00:50:48,206 --> 00:50:50,485
I'm afraid of nothing, Ilbay.

497
00:50:50,766 --> 00:50:53,085
But I always pick my way.

498
00:50:53,606 --> 00:50:57,325
Osman isn't a wolf that you can hold in a cage.

499
00:51:00,286 --> 00:51:02,045
Don't worry, hatun.

500
00:51:02,766 --> 00:51:05,725
Osman will never be able to come back.

501
00:51:06,046 --> 00:51:09,285
If he does, I will kill him myself.

502
00:51:26,806 --> 00:51:28,845
How much further?

503
00:51:29,966 --> 00:51:32,805
There is a stream ahead that feeds the river.

504
00:51:33,806 --> 00:51:37,205
We should take a rest there
before we get out of the borders.

505
00:51:40,046 --> 00:51:42,805
Your words mean nothing here, Osman.

506
00:51:44,606 --> 00:51:48,005
We will have some rest wherever I want.

507
00:51:48,446 --> 00:51:50,325
Well..

508
00:51:51,366 --> 00:51:55,405
Whoever ignores the right words
will hit their heads to the stones!

509
00:51:57,526 --> 00:52:00,085
Nobody else knows this area better than I do.

510
00:52:00,086 --> 00:52:06,325
Yes. You know it well enough
that you can play tricks in it.

511
00:52:09,006 --> 00:52:10,525
What?

512
00:52:10,966 --> 00:52:12,925
Are you afraid of me?

513
00:52:14,166 --> 00:52:16,165
I'm not afraid of you.

514
00:52:16,646 --> 00:52:19,285
I just pity you, Osman.

515
00:52:19,566 --> 00:52:24,885
You still have hopes for
running away but you can't.

516
00:52:25,166 --> 00:52:30,885
I will break your hopes like
the wounds I made in your body.

517
00:52:34,206 --> 00:52:37,765
A Turk is always hope against the dark.

518
00:52:38,566 --> 00:52:42,605
We know how to make the cruel kneel.

519
00:52:44,366 --> 00:52:46,525
Just be patient.

520
00:52:47,766 --> 00:52:50,365
My captivity will be over soon.

521
00:52:50,806 --> 00:52:55,045
Then you will see the dark.

522
00:52:57,166 --> 00:53:01,565
Don't be so sure, Osman. Do not be so sure.

523
00:53:22,566 --> 00:53:25,565
I heard you love Osman, Iltutan...

524
00:53:25,926 --> 00:53:28,565
But I will kill him today.

525
00:53:31,966 --> 00:53:33,645
I know, you..

526
00:53:33,646 --> 00:53:38,325
...think he is a good man. But he is a murderer!

527
00:53:44,806 --> 00:53:47,885
He killed my family, Iltutan!

528
00:53:48,366 --> 00:53:54,045
So you will be an orphan. But don't worry.

529
00:53:54,486 --> 00:53:57,005
I'll take care of you better than him.

530
00:53:58,206 --> 00:54:00,605
Let's go and find Osman.

531
00:54:04,446 --> 00:54:06,485
Sister, isn't that Ilbay a traitor?

532
00:54:06,566 --> 00:54:09,405
Didn't he fool us? Didn't he betray Osman Bey?

533
00:54:09,406 --> 00:54:12,805
How can you say you'll marry him?
-Betrayal for whom, Yusuf?

534
00:54:14,206 --> 00:54:17,805
Ilbay is a Kayi who was treated unfairly.

535
00:54:17,926 --> 00:54:20,445
And he cares about the people more than him.

536
00:54:20,606 --> 00:54:22,285
Sister, what did he say to you?

537
00:54:22,686 --> 00:54:25,125
How did he convince you? How did he trick you?

538
00:54:25,566 --> 00:54:27,325
No one can trick me!

539
00:54:27,606 --> 00:54:29,845
No one can put pressure on me!

540
00:54:30,406 --> 00:54:34,645
We came here with our huge Beylic
and pledged allegiance to Osman.

541
00:54:36,406 --> 00:54:42,965
His impertinent Hatun, Bala
humiliated me and sent me away!

542
00:54:44,126 --> 00:54:48,485
If there is a betrayal, it is
what Osman and his Hatun did.

543
00:54:48,846 --> 00:54:53,885
Sister, look, I am afraid
your grudge will hurt you.

544
00:54:54,686 --> 00:54:56,805
When Osman Bey gets the chair back...

545
00:54:56,806 --> 00:54:58,925
That won't happen.

546
00:55:01,566 --> 00:55:05,525
While I rule state after I marry Ilbay...

547
00:55:07,286 --> 00:55:09,685
...you will grow our Beylic.

548
00:55:10,766 --> 00:55:12,485
Be smart, Yusuf.

549
00:55:13,606 --> 00:55:15,965
I am doing everything for both of us.

550
00:55:20,686 --> 00:55:22,285
Your way is my way, sister.

551
00:55:24,406 --> 00:55:26,045
I will always be by your side

552
00:55:26,166 --> 00:55:27,165
Brother..

553
00:55:37,126 --> 00:55:37,885
Now!

554
00:55:39,286 --> 00:55:41,245
The Righteous!

555
00:55:53,766 --> 00:55:54,525
My Bey..

556
00:55:58,526 --> 00:56:00,045
Osman..

557
00:56:01,006 --> 00:56:04,965
My Bey! My Bey!

558
00:56:07,846 --> 00:56:09,805
Trap!

559
00:56:19,366 --> 00:56:23,205
Trap! Be careful!

560
00:56:33,966 --> 00:56:35,285
Bala!

561
00:56:35,446 --> 00:56:40,365
You found your death while looking for Osman..

562
00:56:40,886 --> 00:56:42,445
Red devil..

563
00:56:44,366 --> 00:56:46,925
You will die before Osman.

564
00:56:47,526 --> 00:56:51,645
Dastard dogs... We will ruin...

565
00:56:51,886 --> 00:56:54,125
...the game you planned here!

566
00:56:54,126 --> 00:56:58,805
We will never fall before
we kill you! Come on Alps!

567
00:56:58,806 --> 00:57:00,485
Allah is the Greatest!

568
00:57:06,606 --> 00:57:08,885
Do not resist for no reason, Bala.

569
00:58:28,366 --> 00:58:30,645
We have a long way to go, Osman.

570
00:58:31,166 --> 00:58:33,445
If you sit there and behave...

571
00:58:33,486 --> 00:58:37,085
...I will take you to Tabriz
without treating you like a dog.

572
00:58:39,446 --> 00:58:42,085
But if you do... -Shut up

573
00:58:44,246 --> 00:58:46,125
Altuga or something...

574
00:58:47,846 --> 00:58:50,285
I will rip that tongue out of your throat.

575
00:58:55,846 --> 00:58:57,205
Osman..

576
00:58:57,446 --> 00:58:59,725
They said you were stubborn.

577
00:59:00,126 --> 00:59:03,965
Look, you lost your state,
but you are still stubborn.

578
00:59:04,806 --> 00:59:07,725
You are a Bey who follows customs. But..

579
00:59:07,966 --> 00:59:09,565
..it's over now.

580
00:59:13,406 --> 00:59:14,685
Ulu Shaman...

581
00:59:15,366 --> 00:59:17,285
...play your qopuz.

582
00:59:17,446 --> 00:59:20,085
Let's make Osman Bey a little happy.

583
01:00:18,566 --> 01:00:21,405
Dog!

584
01:00:21,806 --> 01:00:23,565
What is it?

585
01:00:23,566 --> 01:00:26,365
Did I hurt you?

586
01:00:26,366 --> 01:00:28,725
You dog..

587
01:00:28,726 --> 01:00:29,965
Are you scared?

588
01:00:29,966 --> 01:00:31,765
I told you not to speak!

589
01:00:36,246 --> 01:00:39,525
Of course you are scared,
you are facing Osman Bey!

590
01:00:46,406 --> 01:00:50,605
As long as we have brave warriors like you...

591
01:00:51,326 --> 01:00:54,125
...traitors among us cannot upset us.

592
01:01:02,046 --> 01:01:05,525
This is the dagger of my
grandfather Sungur Tekin...

593
01:01:10,446 --> 01:01:13,685
Thank you Ayse. Thank you.

594
01:02:40,566 --> 01:02:42,445
Osman is running away!

595
01:02:50,766 --> 01:02:52,125
Come on! Catch him!

596
01:03:21,206 --> 01:03:24,565
You say the same thing every
time my sword touches yours.

597
01:03:24,566 --> 01:03:26,805
But I will not die before I kill you.

598
01:03:26,806 --> 01:03:29,485
You will not die easily, Bala.

599
01:03:29,486 --> 01:03:31,125
You will beg me.

600
01:03:39,926 --> 01:03:41,165
Did that hurt?

601
01:04:51,486 --> 01:04:53,365
Are you still planning games?

602
01:04:53,366 --> 01:04:55,805
It is the only truth of your life!

603
01:05:07,926 --> 01:05:11,925
We are stepping back! Come on!

604
01:05:17,886 --> 01:05:22,005
We are stepping back! Come on!

605
01:05:44,766 --> 01:05:46,485
Attack!

606
01:05:46,486 --> 01:05:50,805
-Don't let them run away!
-They won't be able to escape! Attack!

607
01:06:14,726 --> 01:06:17,085
You will never be able to escape, Osman.

608
01:06:17,086 --> 01:06:18,085
Never.

609
01:07:44,526 --> 01:07:50,645
So you ran away Osman... But I swear...

610
01:07:53,086 --> 01:07:55,125
..I will kill you.

611
01:08:21,486 --> 01:08:23,085
Noker(Mongolian Soldiers) Uncle.

612
01:08:25,126 --> 01:08:26,965
I am Ilbay Bey's daughter.

613
01:08:27,246 --> 01:08:30,965
I am giving everyone sherbet
because my father is the new Bey.

614
01:08:35,526 --> 01:08:37,045
Drink some.

615
01:09:21,606 --> 01:09:22,925
Ghazi.

616
01:09:24,645 --> 01:09:27,805
I know I am late...
But I could not come before.

617
01:09:35,526 --> 01:09:39,165
Did you know your father was a traitor, Ayse?

618
01:09:42,606 --> 01:09:43,925
Stop..

619
01:09:43,926 --> 01:09:47,245
Let's untie this knot. We have to escape.

620
01:09:49,606 --> 01:09:53,524
You always told me "If you knew who I was..."..

621
01:09:54,366 --> 01:09:55,925
This was why, right?

622
01:09:56,886 --> 01:09:59,405
You knew you were a Kayi

623
01:10:05,646 --> 01:10:07,365
I knew it.

624
01:10:07,726 --> 01:10:10,845
But I did not know my
father was a traitor, Ghazi.

625
01:10:11,126 --> 01:10:14,845
If I knew, wouldn't I tell
you and our Osman Bey?

626
01:10:18,886 --> 01:10:23,445
You are far away from your father
and mother because of my father.

627
01:10:24,126 --> 01:10:28,125
I will not get mad at you
even if you don't believe me.

628
01:10:28,526 --> 01:10:30,765
It's not about my father or mother, Ayse.

629
01:10:31,006 --> 01:10:33,165
We are losing our state.

630
01:10:35,526 --> 01:10:37,965
We need to save Osman Bey, come on.

631
01:10:40,726 --> 01:10:45,285
Before they took my Osman
Bey, I secretly gave him a dagger.

632
01:10:45,526 --> 01:10:48,285
So maybe he could save himself.

633
01:10:49,846 --> 01:10:51,965
Halal to you Ayse.

634
01:10:52,286 --> 01:10:55,365
I swear you will be a brave Alp.

635
01:10:55,806 --> 01:10:57,525
I will not be an Alp!

636
01:10:57,526 --> 01:10:59,365
I will be a Sister!

637
01:11:00,086 --> 01:11:01,765
Like Bala Hatun.

638
01:11:07,726 --> 01:11:08,805
Come on.

639
01:11:10,766 --> 01:11:14,565
We must escape before the effect
of the sherbet wears off. Let's go!

640
01:11:14,566 --> 01:11:15,725
You are right.

641
01:11:21,646 --> 01:11:23,005
Tie Ghazi up.

642
01:11:23,606 --> 01:11:25,125
Ayse will come with me.

643
01:11:25,806 --> 01:11:27,885
Don't touch me!

644
01:11:27,886 --> 01:11:29,965
Let me go!

645
01:11:29,966 --> 01:11:36,485
No! No! Osman Bey will make
you pay for this! Let me go!

646
01:11:36,486 --> 01:11:39,725
Let me go!

647
01:12:11,086 --> 01:12:14,525
Come at us, you infidel dogs. 
O Righteous!

648
01:12:27,606 --> 01:12:28,885
Go after them!

649
01:12:28,886 --> 01:12:30,925
No one will survive here!

650
01:12:30,926 --> 01:12:32,725
Go after them

651
01:12:50,246 --> 01:12:53,005
Pick every stone up! Look everywhere

652
01:12:54,046 --> 01:12:56,765
Osman is not far away,
he is around here! Come on!

653
01:13:07,766 --> 01:13:09,645
Where did you hide, Osman?

654
01:13:10,446 --> 01:13:17,045
Where are you? Iltutan, stop! Stop! Iltutan!

655
01:13:17,046 --> 01:13:18,125
Iltutan, be quiet!

656
01:13:19,206 --> 01:13:22,525
Iltutan!

657
01:14:01,926 --> 01:14:03,365
There are tracks here.

658
01:14:03,366 --> 01:14:08,525
This way!

659
01:14:20,846 --> 01:14:22,125
Search everywhere!

660
01:14:23,166 --> 01:14:25,765
Noises come from this side! Come on!

661
01:14:36,086 --> 01:14:38,925
Osman.

662
01:14:46,806 --> 01:14:48,885
So you are here, Osman.

663
01:14:51,726 --> 01:14:53,565
It's over now, Osman.

664
01:14:53,766 --> 01:14:56,045
There is no tomorrow for you.

665
01:14:58,526 --> 01:15:00,605
Today, I am Azrael.

666
01:15:01,806 --> 01:15:09,845
Today is the day of your death.

667
01:15:12,046 --> 01:15:13,285
She is going to Osman!

668
01:15:13,286 --> 01:15:16,005
She is one of Osman's people! Kill her!

669
01:15:38,646 --> 01:15:41,365
Meryem! My daughter!

670
01:15:42,326 --> 01:15:46,685
Come here. Come.

671
01:16:03,246 --> 01:16:05,365
We've put quite a distance between us.

672
01:16:05,366 --> 01:16:07,565
They lost our trail, but we can't stop.

673
01:16:07,566 --> 01:16:09,845
We need to find out which
direction they took Osman Bey.

674
01:16:09,846 --> 01:16:12,205
The real trap must be set along the road.

675
01:16:12,886 --> 01:16:16,285
Mother, only two roads lead to Tabriz now.

676
01:16:17,646 --> 01:16:21,165
The Saricali road is quite
winding, it will slow us down.

677
01:16:21,446 --> 01:16:25,005
Kizilkayalar, on the other hand,
passes through the swamp, Alaeddin.

678
01:16:25,086 --> 01:16:28,605
They must have taken serious
precautions to protect my father.

679
01:16:28,686 --> 01:16:31,885
Why would so many nokers
(Mongolian Soldiers) go through the swamp?

680
01:16:32,006 --> 01:16:34,765
We can no longer be sure
of anything. These devils...

681
01:16:34,766 --> 01:16:37,125
...might have used both routes to mislead us.

682
01:16:37,126 --> 01:16:39,765
The best way is to split
up and search both ways.

683
01:16:39,766 --> 01:16:43,165
That way, we won't lose time either, right?
-You are right my Orhan.

684
01:16:43,166 --> 01:16:48,165
Then, Alaeddin, you and
the girls take the Saricali route.

685
01:16:48,166 --> 01:16:49,765
Turhan will go with you.

686
01:16:49,766 --> 01:16:54,125
Cerkutay will lead us through Kizilkayalar
without taking us into the swamp.

687
01:16:54,166 --> 01:16:56,485
Boran, Aykut, you will come with me.

688
01:16:56,486 --> 01:16:58,565
-As you order Bala Hatun.
-Okay.

689
01:16:59,086 --> 01:17:02,365
Come on! Let's not waste
time! May Allah be with you!

690
01:17:06,006 --> 01:17:07,365
Come on!

691
01:17:11,846 --> 01:17:12,885
Come on

692
01:17:22,846 --> 01:17:25,045
Meryem, what are you doing here?

693
01:17:25,046 --> 01:17:27,805
I ran away from the tribe, my Bey.

694
01:17:27,886 --> 01:17:31,805
I wanted to help you, but I couldn't...

695
01:17:31,806 --> 01:17:34,925
I see. I see.

696
01:17:34,926 --> 01:17:38,205
I understood you were
brave when I first saw you.

697
01:17:42,726 --> 01:17:44,085
Here...

698
01:17:45,486 --> 01:17:48,325
But my Bey... You are also hurt.

699
01:17:50,446 --> 01:17:54,205
I will only slow you down
while Mongols are after us.

700
01:17:54,606 --> 01:17:56,085
Why do you say that?

701
01:17:56,086 --> 01:18:00,165
Is my life more precious than yours? Huh?
-True, but..

702
01:18:00,726 --> 01:18:02,205
...because of the antidote...

703
01:18:03,686 --> 01:18:07,405
You are in this situation because of us.
-Don't worry.

704
01:18:07,486 --> 01:18:09,125
Nothing will happen to us.

705
01:18:09,126 --> 01:18:12,005
Hang on now. I will break the arrow.

706
01:18:15,646 --> 01:18:17,045
Did that hurt a lot?

707
01:18:17,446 --> 01:18:18,765
Yes, my Bey.

708
01:18:19,566 --> 01:18:21,165
Alright.

709
01:18:21,166 --> 01:18:24,885
We need to find herbs to ease your pain.

710
01:18:25,126 --> 01:18:27,245
Come, let's go somewhere hidden.

711
01:18:27,246 --> 01:18:28,405
Come.

712
01:18:48,486 --> 01:18:49,565
My Ayse..

713
01:18:51,686 --> 01:18:54,085
My daughter, why are you doing this?

714
01:18:54,206 --> 01:18:57,845
Because my father taught me honesty and bravery!

715
01:18:58,046 --> 01:19:00,525
Why are you doing this?!

716
01:19:05,766 --> 01:19:06,925
Look, my daughter.

717
01:19:07,926 --> 01:19:11,685
I am doing everything to take what is ours.

718
01:19:13,006 --> 01:19:14,645
I deserve this chair.

719
01:19:16,046 --> 01:19:18,645
And after me, it will belong to your children.

720
01:19:18,926 --> 01:19:20,125
I don't want it.

721
01:19:20,686 --> 01:19:24,725
Those bad men...
Mongols... They kill everyone!

722
01:19:25,006 --> 01:19:27,325
And they are keeping Ghazi as a prisoner!

723
01:19:27,326 --> 01:19:29,965
And they will martyr our Osman Bey!

724
01:19:31,326 --> 01:19:35,325
And you are uniting with
them! And you say it's our right!

725
01:19:35,326 --> 01:19:38,165
Are we going to get what's
ours by betraying others?!

726
01:19:40,006 --> 01:19:42,045
My daughter, this is not betrayal.

727
01:19:42,206 --> 01:19:45,685
What Osman did is actual betrayal.

728
01:19:47,486 --> 01:19:49,125
You don't understand me now.

729
01:19:50,006 --> 01:19:53,245
But when you grow up, you
will say your father was right.

730
01:19:53,286 --> 01:19:54,645
My father?

731
01:19:55,406 --> 01:19:58,565
My father would never let others oppress Turks!

732
01:19:58,966 --> 01:20:00,765
I don't know you!

733
01:20:00,766 --> 01:20:03,485
You are not my father! -My Ayse!

734
01:20:12,806 --> 01:20:14,205
My Bey.

735
01:20:15,566 --> 01:20:18,245
You are the heir of Sungur Tegin.

736
01:20:19,166 --> 01:20:21,485
If a Kayi Bey is to sit on the chair

737
01:20:22,446 --> 01:20:26,005
...it shouldn't be Osman but you.

738
01:20:31,646 --> 01:20:35,365
Even if you don't do it for
yourself, do it for your daughter.

739
01:20:38,126 --> 01:20:42,565
-For the only thing left from your wife.
-Never. The chair is Osman Bey's.

740
01:20:44,366 --> 01:20:47,565
This dagger and little Ayse are enough for me.

741
01:20:50,166 --> 01:20:52,445
I won't betray my kin.

742
01:21:07,406 --> 01:21:10,565
If you don't, I will.

743
01:21:31,526 --> 01:21:35,805
I'm now Ilbay, grandson of Sungur Tegin.

744
01:21:41,526 --> 01:21:43,485
And you are my daughter.

745
01:21:48,966 --> 01:21:50,645
Ayse, my daughter.

746
01:21:54,606 --> 01:21:57,165
We've kept our secret together so far.

747
01:21:58,446 --> 01:22:00,365
We've gone through a lot.

748
01:22:01,246 --> 01:22:03,525
It's all because of Osman.

749
01:22:17,566 --> 01:22:21,685
You asked me why we kept this dagger.

750
01:22:30,326 --> 01:22:32,685
If Osman had known we had the dagger.

751
01:22:33,326 --> 01:22:35,565
...he'd have killed both you and me.

752
01:22:41,846 --> 01:22:43,925
This dagger...

753
01:23:00,446 --> 01:23:02,525
Where is the dagger?

754
01:23:05,166 --> 01:23:07,085
I gave it to Osman Bey.

755
01:23:07,806 --> 01:23:11,405
-So he could save himself.
-What did you do, Ayse?

756
01:23:20,086 --> 01:23:22,645
You've gone too far this time.

757
01:23:28,046 --> 01:23:29,405
Stay here.

758
01:24:04,166 --> 01:24:05,645
I swear...

759
01:24:06,286 --> 01:24:09,805
...I will get those rebels
executed in this square.

760
01:24:10,566 --> 01:24:14,445
They can't go anywhere
now. They are all in need.

761
01:24:15,046 --> 01:24:17,725
They will fall into our claws.

762
01:24:19,366 --> 01:24:20,925
Ulugan.

763
01:24:25,686 --> 01:24:27,365
Osman.

764
01:24:28,806 --> 01:24:30,565
What about him?

765
01:24:31,646 --> 01:24:33,005
My daughter Ayse...

766
01:24:33,566 --> 01:24:37,445
...gave Osman a dagger when she hugged him.

767
01:24:41,046 --> 01:24:44,725
He can't get out of the cage with
the dagger but you should know.

768
01:24:50,686 --> 01:24:52,645
What are you talking about, Ilbay?

769
01:24:54,806 --> 01:24:56,845
Are you hearing yourself?

770
01:24:58,726 --> 01:25:02,205
Just as Osman was going to our Khan,

771
01:25:02,486 --> 01:25:06,645
...your kid gave him a dagger
to help him escape, huh?

772
01:25:11,166 --> 01:25:13,605
If Osman escapes

773
01:25:13,966 --> 01:25:18,485
...my credibility will be
ruined before Olcaytu Khan.

774
01:25:19,166 --> 01:25:22,205
And your head won't stand on your shoulders!

775
01:25:22,286 --> 01:25:25,125
He can't escape while
Altuga is there. Don't worry.

776
01:25:28,686 --> 01:25:30,125
Nokers(Mongolian Soldiers)!

777
01:25:37,846 --> 01:25:43,445
Go warn Altuga to be careful! Now!

778
01:25:53,966 --> 01:25:57,005
If we can't find Osman Ulugan will kill us all!

779
01:25:57,086 --> 01:25:59,605
Search everywhere! Everywhere!

780
01:26:11,526 --> 01:26:13,085
There's blood here.

781
01:26:13,446 --> 01:26:14,805
Blood here!

782
01:26:23,606 --> 01:26:24,965
Osman.

783
01:26:25,326 --> 01:26:27,125
Where are you going, Osman?

784
01:26:27,446 --> 01:26:30,765
You can't go much further
with your wound. Nokers(Mongolian Soldiers)!

785
01:26:30,806 --> 01:26:33,885
Osman will try to spend
the night in an isolated place.

786
01:26:34,086 --> 01:26:37,725
Caves and pits... Leave no stones unturned!

787
01:26:46,966 --> 01:26:50,445
Come, hold on. Come on.

788
01:26:50,486 --> 01:26:53,445
Hold on, hold on.

789
01:26:53,806 --> 01:26:57,285
-We need to find a safe place.
-I can hold on.

790
01:27:14,686 --> 01:27:16,485
Iltutan.

791
01:27:19,086 --> 01:27:20,525
Iltutan.

792
01:27:24,126 --> 01:27:25,805
Come here.

793
01:27:26,726 --> 01:27:28,365
My Iltutan.

794
01:27:29,046 --> 01:27:30,805
What are you doing here?

795
01:27:31,126 --> 01:27:33,365
I brought Iltutan here, my Bey.

796
01:27:34,166 --> 01:27:37,645
-But we got separated.
-What?

797
01:27:41,126 --> 01:27:42,725
How come?

798
01:27:43,446 --> 01:27:45,685
How could he let you ride him?

799
01:27:46,566 --> 01:27:47,645
I don't know.

800
01:27:48,286 --> 01:27:50,125
He didn't show bad temper.

801
01:27:55,366 --> 01:27:57,125
Iltutan..

802
01:27:58,646 --> 01:28:01,765
He wouldn't let anyone ride him.

803
01:28:14,446 --> 01:28:16,365
Look at me.

804
01:28:17,886 --> 01:28:19,445
Iltutan.

805
01:28:19,766 --> 01:28:26,485
Well... He knows where to stop and who to help.

806
01:28:30,366 --> 01:28:32,685
Come on, let's go.

807
01:28:32,886 --> 01:28:34,925
We need to find a safe place.

808
01:28:35,046 --> 01:28:36,685
Come on.

809
01:28:43,966 --> 01:28:46,925
Mongolian dastards always leave tracks behind.

810
01:28:47,046 --> 01:28:50,045
But there are no tracks here.

811
01:28:50,166 --> 01:28:53,965
Ulugan isn't like the ones we saw before.

812
01:28:54,046 --> 01:28:56,925
He's not. We need to be cautious.

813
01:28:57,526 --> 01:29:01,165
We will either find a way or make our own way.

814
01:29:01,406 --> 01:29:03,965
But we have to save Osman Bey somehow.

815
01:29:05,086 --> 01:29:07,925
Orhan. Let me check your wound.

816
01:29:08,806 --> 01:29:11,613
It's not a big deal,
Holofira. I'm good.

817
01:29:11,625 --> 01:29:12,565
You're not.

818
01:29:15,206 --> 01:29:19,765
Brother, let's have some
rest. We can't go on like this.

819
01:29:20,046 --> 01:29:22,365
We should examine your wounds.

820
01:29:22,766 --> 01:29:25,325
I'll spread this ointment on your wounds.

821
01:29:28,286 --> 01:29:29,725
I will do it.

822
01:29:30,526 --> 01:29:31,885
Alright.

823
01:29:33,566 --> 01:29:35,885
-Come on.
-Ayaz! Yagiz!

824
01:29:36,046 --> 01:29:37,805
Watch around.

825
01:29:38,086 --> 01:29:41,285
-We'll take some rest and continue.
-As you order, my Bey.

826
01:29:52,166 --> 01:29:54,005
You will be alright.

827
01:30:14,926 --> 01:30:18,805
Holofira, this wound...

828
01:30:19,846 --> 01:30:21,645
It's nothing.

829
01:30:24,126 --> 01:30:25,885
My father...

830
01:30:26,686 --> 01:30:28,405
...was taken captive...

831
01:30:29,646 --> 01:30:31,925
...to save me because of me.

832
01:30:33,606 --> 01:30:38,365
This wound is nothing
compared to the fire inside me.

833
01:30:41,686 --> 01:30:45,605
We'll save father and take our tribe back.

834
01:30:46,126 --> 01:30:50,125
Beyond believing, I'm sure of this.

835
01:30:52,406 --> 01:30:55,005
Just like I knew you'd come back.

836
01:30:57,366 --> 01:30:59,365
God willing, Holofira.

837
01:30:59,806 --> 01:31:01,325
God willing.

838
01:31:04,126 --> 01:31:06,645
We will heal all our wounds.

839
01:31:21,006 --> 01:31:22,285
God gave us

840
01:31:23,686 --> 01:31:27,285
...such a gift in such a time.

841
01:31:27,726 --> 01:31:29,405
It means hope.

842
01:31:30,846 --> 01:31:32,485
It's a message.

843
01:31:33,006 --> 01:31:34,965
Holofira.

844
01:31:46,126 --> 01:31:47,925
My Holofira.

845
01:31:48,366 --> 01:31:51,365
My daylight... My sun.

846
01:31:52,686 --> 01:31:58,005
Is this... Do I get it right?

847
01:31:58,246 --> 01:32:03,445
-I am...
You're going to be a father.

848
01:32:03,806 --> 01:32:05,565
I'm pregnant.

849
01:32:07,166 --> 01:32:09,965
You and I are going to have a baby.

850
01:32:19,926 --> 01:32:21,805
Thanks to Allah.

851
01:32:22,806 --> 01:32:24,805
Thanks to Allah.

852
01:32:30,926 --> 01:32:34,125
My daylight... My sun...

853
01:32:34,406 --> 01:32:36,365
My love.

854
01:32:37,526 --> 01:32:40,205
The one who gives me strength with love.

855
01:32:41,806 --> 01:32:45,645
You gave me such great news...

856
01:32:46,286 --> 01:32:48,845
You gave me life.

857
01:32:57,806 --> 01:32:59,885
When we save my father

858
01:33:00,206 --> 01:33:04,765
...I swear we'll make
all the cruel ones kneel...

859
01:33:06,606 --> 01:33:09,205
...and shake this world together.

860
01:33:09,366 --> 01:33:11,005
I know.

861
01:33:11,606 --> 01:33:13,925
Everything is possible with you.

862
01:33:38,086 --> 01:33:40,805
Death is looming over Kayi.

863
01:33:41,406 --> 01:33:43,125
Some ran away.

864
01:33:44,726 --> 01:33:46,605
They are uneasy too.

865
01:33:47,286 --> 01:33:49,325
What about the ones in the tribe?

866
01:33:51,726 --> 01:33:53,205
What about my Ghazi?

867
01:33:53,726 --> 01:33:56,045
Who knows how they are doing?

868
01:33:56,446 --> 01:34:00,125
Brother... Ghazi was trained by you, Cerkutay.

869
01:34:00,726 --> 01:34:03,765
He can beat even their best ones.

870
01:34:04,366 --> 01:34:07,245
Don't worry, brother.

871
01:34:07,766 --> 01:34:11,365
You and your son will come
together soon, God willing.

872
01:34:12,606 --> 01:34:14,125
God willing.

873
01:34:16,686 --> 01:34:20,005
I will sacrifice my life if I have
to but I'll take my son back.

874
01:34:21,206 --> 01:34:24,205
But we need to find our Bey first.

875
01:34:25,646 --> 01:34:28,125
Don't fall into despair but be patient.

876
01:34:28,406 --> 01:34:31,325
We'll always carry our
grief in our hearts, but...

877
01:34:31,686 --> 01:34:34,005
...we'll make Mongolians pay for this.

878
01:34:34,166 --> 01:34:37,725
When Osman Bey is saved,
they all will burn in flames.

879
01:34:38,246 --> 01:34:44,005
We'll make them pay for every
wound they opened inside us.

880
01:34:48,526 --> 01:34:52,125
Cerkutay, check these trails. What is this?

881
01:34:52,326 --> 01:34:53,965
Is it Osman Bey?

882
01:34:54,126 --> 01:34:56,925
Brother, check this out.

883
01:35:02,726 --> 01:35:06,965
Cart tracks... Still fresh.

884
01:35:12,286 --> 01:35:14,565
There are also horses beside the cart.

885
01:35:14,726 --> 01:35:18,085
The horse shoes were made
by Mongolian ironmongers.

886
01:35:23,566 --> 01:35:25,405
It may be them.

887
01:35:27,206 --> 01:35:29,645
Which way have they gone? We should follow.

888
01:35:30,526 --> 01:35:32,765
This way, Bala Hatun.

889
01:35:32,846 --> 01:35:36,165
-Come on then.
-Let's go, brother.

890
01:35:37,166 --> 01:35:38,725
Let's go, alps!

891
01:35:40,886 --> 01:35:44,805
Come on, come on! I'm coming, Osman.

892
01:35:44,886 --> 01:35:46,925
Come on!

893
01:35:54,366 --> 01:35:56,605
The fire is ready.

894
01:36:03,846 --> 01:36:05,245
Meryem.

895
01:36:05,926 --> 01:36:07,885
Here we go.

896
01:36:09,446 --> 01:36:14,045
Take this. You bite this for the pain.

897
01:36:15,766 --> 01:36:21,165
Well... This will hurt a lot.

898
01:36:22,606 --> 01:36:24,205
But you need to endure.

899
01:36:24,886 --> 01:36:27,685
I can endure, my Bey.

900
01:36:30,486 --> 01:36:34,605
Press my hand if it goes wrong, alright?

901
01:36:39,366 --> 01:36:44,605
Here we go. In the name of Allah,
the compassionate, the merciful.

902
01:36:44,806 --> 01:36:46,965
Hold on, hold on.

903
01:36:51,286 --> 01:36:52,725
Hang on!

904
01:36:52,806 --> 01:36:56,565
Hang on, hang on! Hang on!

905
01:37:02,526 --> 01:37:05,685
Look at me. Look.

906
01:37:06,166 --> 01:37:08,085
I will cauterize it now.

907
01:37:08,326 --> 01:37:11,365
It will hurt a lot. Worse
than any pain you know.

908
01:37:11,446 --> 01:37:13,205
Here we go.

909
01:37:16,166 --> 01:37:18,485
O Healer.

910
01:37:22,446 --> 01:37:26,445
Hang on, girl. Hang on.

911
01:37:34,566 --> 01:37:38,325
Well... You are....

912
01:37:38,446 --> 01:37:43,805
You are so strong. Very strong.

913
01:37:45,046 --> 01:37:48,245
It's obvious you're from these lands.

914
01:37:52,766 --> 01:37:55,445
We don't know whose your parents are, but...

915
01:37:57,086 --> 01:37:59,325
...I wish I knew them.

916
01:38:00,566 --> 01:38:02,005
I wish.

917
01:38:02,686 --> 01:38:06,925
I wish I did. If a cruel man hadn't killed them

918
01:38:07,406 --> 01:38:09,565
..I would know them.

919
01:38:35,806 --> 01:38:39,965
What about your father? Don't
you know anything about him?

920
01:39:09,326 --> 01:39:10,925
Then..

921
01:39:11,646 --> 01:39:13,765
...jackal...

922
01:39:14,766 --> 01:39:16,645
...jackal..

923
01:39:16,646 --> 01:39:19,405
...approached the gazelle...

924
01:39:19,846 --> 01:39:24,085
...quietly, and said:

925
01:39:25,566 --> 01:39:27,205
"Gazelle..

926
01:39:27,686 --> 01:39:31,365
...do not wander around here...

927
01:39:31,606 --> 01:39:32,885
Or else...

928
01:39:32,886 --> 01:39:36,045
...they will abduct you."

929
01:39:36,526 --> 01:39:38,205
He said "Come...

930
01:39:38,206 --> 01:39:40,845
Let me take you to your house."

931
01:39:41,526 --> 01:39:45,525
Did she go?
-No.

932
01:39:45,646 --> 01:39:47,445
Little gazelle...

933
01:39:48,606 --> 01:39:51,965
..was a bit afraid. She was afraid...

934
01:39:51,966 --> 01:39:53,525
...but she was smart.

935
01:39:53,526 --> 01:39:55,205
She said "No, no...

936
01:39:55,206 --> 01:39:58,205
I will not come with you!"

937
01:39:59,326 --> 01:40:01,765
Jackal, after hearing this...

938
01:40:01,766 --> 01:40:07,325
...set his eyes on the gazelle!

939
01:40:11,166 --> 01:40:15,485
Was she afraid? Was she alone?

940
01:40:15,686 --> 01:40:19,565
The gazelle, yes she was afraid.

941
01:40:20,326 --> 01:40:24,325
But deep in the forest...

942
01:40:26,846 --> 01:40:31,645
...there was a wolf watching them. The wolf...

943
01:40:31,646 --> 01:40:34,525
...would never let someone...

944
01:40:34,526 --> 01:40:37,285
...hurt the gazelle.

945
01:40:38,326 --> 01:40:39,485
The wolf..

946
01:40:39,486 --> 01:40:41,765
...kept watching them.

947
01:40:43,246 --> 01:40:46,245
The gazelle, who was scared, said:

948
01:40:46,246 --> 01:40:50,045
O, the guardian of the forest!

949
01:40:50,046 --> 01:40:52,165
Will you help me?

950
01:40:52,566 --> 01:40:54,685
After hearing this, the wolf...

951
01:40:54,686 --> 01:40:57,005
...leaped forward

952
01:40:57,006 --> 01:40:59,365
Ssht...

953
01:40:59,366 --> 01:41:01,685
"What is happening here?", he said...

954
01:41:01,846 --> 01:41:05,005
"Where are you?", he said to the jackal.

955
01:41:08,646 --> 01:41:12,765
After hearing this, the jackal
did not know what to do.

956
01:41:12,766 --> 01:41:19,205
"No, no, no.", he said...

957
01:41:19,206 --> 01:41:20,965
...and he started running away.

958
01:41:22,126 --> 01:41:24,725
My Halime...

959
01:41:24,726 --> 01:41:27,365
Did you lose your sleep again, my daughter?

960
01:41:37,086 --> 01:41:38,885
She had her sleep...

961
01:41:39,086 --> 01:41:40,765
But it ran away to the forest...

962
01:41:41,566 --> 01:41:44,165
Did you find it?

963
01:41:44,166 --> 01:41:49,125
Yes, we did. We did, right, my daughter?

964
01:41:50,646 --> 01:41:54,525
Come on now, kiss your father. Kiss your father.

965
01:41:59,726 --> 01:42:01,685
Isn't there another tale?

966
01:42:02,446 --> 01:42:04,765
We heard enough tales.

967
01:42:04,846 --> 01:42:06,885
Come, come here.

968
01:42:07,126 --> 01:42:08,125
Come on.

969
01:42:08,126 --> 01:42:10,765
The wolf protected the little gazelle...

970
01:42:11,326 --> 01:42:15,605
Now it is time for the little
gazelle to sleep, my daughter.

971
01:42:15,606 --> 01:42:16,805
Right, her father?

972
01:42:16,806 --> 01:42:19,925
Sure, or else the jackal will follow her!

973
01:42:20,006 --> 01:42:21,885
The jackal is coming, run, Halime!

974
01:42:21,966 --> 01:42:22,525
Run, run

975
01:42:23,726 --> 01:42:26,885
I'm coming! I'm coming! I'm coming!

976
01:42:33,926 --> 01:42:35,565
My daughter...

977
01:43:07,606 --> 01:43:08,845
The wolf..

978
01:43:09,166 --> 01:43:11,325
...could not protect that gazelle.

979
01:43:13,526 --> 01:43:15,365
Then the gazelle...

980
01:43:17,246 --> 01:43:21,565
...turned into a bird and flew away.

981
01:43:26,966 --> 01:43:29,405
So, you like shadow plays, huh, Meryem?

982
01:43:31,206 --> 01:43:32,245
I don't know.

983
01:43:33,126 --> 01:43:34,685
I do it sometimes.

984
01:43:35,646 --> 01:43:37,405
I don't know why...

985
01:43:37,886 --> 01:43:40,325
...but I feel happy when I do it.

986
01:43:42,006 --> 01:43:43,765
It feels like...

987
01:43:44,166 --> 01:43:47,525
...there was a moment long
ago when I was this happy.

988
01:43:47,806 --> 01:43:49,525
There is a moment...

989
01:43:49,726 --> 01:43:52,205
...that everyone feels happy.

990
01:43:55,046 --> 01:43:58,805
How do you know so much about shadow plays?

991
01:43:59,566 --> 01:44:00,645
My daughter...

992
01:44:07,526 --> 01:44:08,645
My daughter...

993
01:44:10,726 --> 01:44:12,925
...used to wait for her father every night.

994
01:44:14,846 --> 01:44:16,525
She really loved shadow play.

995
01:44:16,526 --> 01:44:19,925
She always waited for me to come and do it.

996
01:44:22,886 --> 01:44:23,965
My daughter...

997
01:44:27,526 --> 01:44:30,045
My Halime...

998
01:44:42,326 --> 01:44:44,645
We lost her when she was so little...

999
01:44:50,966 --> 01:44:52,085
If she...

1000
01:44:52,286 --> 01:44:54,445
...if she lived...

1001
01:44:55,446 --> 01:44:58,125
...she would probably be the same age as you.

1002
01:45:03,766 --> 01:45:06,725
Are you defending Osman right now, Poena?

1003
01:45:09,446 --> 01:45:13,445
The man who killed your mother and father..

1004
01:45:14,806 --> 01:45:19,005
...and left you alone between those bodies?

1005
01:45:32,686 --> 01:45:34,525
There is another cave ahead!

1006
01:45:44,966 --> 01:45:48,645
This horse... This is Osman's horse.

1007
01:45:51,246 --> 01:45:53,725
Be quiet.

1008
01:46:09,246 --> 01:46:10,565
Ohh my daughter...

1009
01:46:12,606 --> 01:46:15,405
You are carrying a big
burden at such a young age.

1010
01:46:16,966 --> 01:46:18,685
You don't have a family as well...

1011
01:46:19,606 --> 01:46:22,125
But their prayers will always protect you.

1012
01:46:23,446 --> 01:46:24,485
Besides...

1013
01:46:26,086 --> 01:46:27,765
...little gazelles...

1014
01:46:28,046 --> 01:46:30,445
...are never alone.

1015
01:46:38,766 --> 01:46:40,565
My daughter...

1016
01:46:40,926 --> 01:46:43,285
Blood, blood, blood...

1017
01:46:43,286 --> 01:46:45,045
Inform Ulugan.

1018
01:46:45,406 --> 01:46:47,485
Osman ran away but...

1019
01:46:47,526 --> 01:46:49,405
...Altuga caught him.

1020
01:46:49,446 --> 01:46:53,805
Tell him I will take him to Olcaytu. Go.

1021
01:46:54,006 --> 01:46:57,725
They found us. They want me.

1022
01:46:57,726 --> 01:46:59,485
You will stay here.

1023
01:46:59,646 --> 01:47:02,725
I can protect myself.

1024
01:47:02,726 --> 01:47:05,805
When I am here, I will protect you. Don't worry.

1025
01:47:05,806 --> 01:47:07,965
You will do as I say.

1026
01:47:09,126 --> 01:47:09,855
Osman

1027
01:47:09,855 --> 01:47:10,885
Blood blood blood!

1028
01:47:10,885 --> 01:47:13,925
You are trapped like a wounded wolf...

1029
01:47:13,966 --> 01:47:15,885
...but come out!

1030
01:47:16,246 --> 01:47:18,045
Come out Osman!

1031
01:47:18,046 --> 01:47:19,885
Don't be afraid, come!

1032
01:47:20,566 --> 01:47:24,845
Look, I know what they
want. They cannot kill me.

1033
01:47:24,966 --> 01:47:26,805
But they can kill you.

1034
01:47:27,086 --> 01:47:28,205
What about you...

1035
01:47:28,686 --> 01:47:31,845
What are you going to do, Osman Bey?
-Don't worry.

1036
01:47:32,086 --> 01:47:35,285
I will go out. I will waste their time.

1037
01:47:35,446 --> 01:47:36,725
But you...

1038
01:47:36,846 --> 01:47:39,885
Don't feel upset because you have no one.

1039
01:47:39,886 --> 01:47:46,125
Find Bala Hatun. You will run away while
I waste their time. She will protect you.

1040
01:47:47,206 --> 01:47:49,485
Come on now.

1041
01:47:58,505 --> 01:48:08,365
Blood! Blood! Blood!

1042
01:48:08,526 --> 01:48:13,845
You made us chase you, but again,
you are at the end of the way, Osman.

1043
01:48:19,406 --> 01:48:24,165
If a wolf does not make forty jackals howl
behind him, he cannot be called a wolf.

1044
01:48:24,206 --> 01:48:26,405
You have been running...

1045
01:48:27,646 --> 01:48:30,205
So you will die tired

1046
01:48:30,206 --> 01:48:34,005
I will take you to Olcaytu safely, but...

1047
01:48:34,006 --> 01:48:37,765
...I will break every bone in your body, Osman.

1048
01:48:38,166 --> 01:48:44,045
Nokers(Mongolian Soldiers),
break Osman's arms and legs separately!

1049
01:48:44,046 --> 01:48:45,045
Come on

1050
01:49:03,846 --> 01:49:07,125
God, why is this happening?

1051
01:49:07,126 --> 01:49:09,725
Why is my heart filled with worry?

1052
01:49:10,526 --> 01:49:13,405
Why do I want to help him?

1053
01:49:14,046 --> 01:49:15,005
Why?

1054
01:49:25,926 --> 01:49:27,205
If you lock the wolf...

1055
01:49:28,446 --> 01:49:30,405
..in a cage...

1056
01:49:31,246 --> 01:49:33,765
...you must take its swords.

1057
01:49:36,846 --> 01:49:39,045
You will cut off its claws.

1058
01:49:40,526 --> 01:49:42,565
You will tear out its teeth.

1059
01:49:49,606 --> 01:49:53,685
Otherwise, if you reach out your hand...

1060
01:49:56,326 --> 01:49:58,005
...it will rip off your arm.

1061
01:50:08,046 --> 01:50:10,885
Your daughter, Ilbay...

1062
01:50:11,166 --> 01:50:13,085
She gave a sword to the wolf.

1063
01:50:13,766 --> 01:50:15,325
And she became his hope.

1064
01:50:17,486 --> 01:50:21,965
My knights have spread out on both
sides of the Kayi Germiyan border.

1065
01:50:22,166 --> 01:50:26,525
Even if he escapes from that cage, he
won't be able to escape from our hands.

1066
01:50:27,406 --> 01:50:30,965
Do not forget we are talking about Osman, Lukas.

1067
01:50:32,406 --> 01:50:36,045
Since Bala and his Shahzades ran away from us...

1068
01:50:38,006 --> 01:50:39,925
...do not underestimate him.

1069
01:50:39,926 --> 01:50:42,005
We will catch them all Sofia.

1070
01:50:43,806 --> 01:50:45,565
Ulugan's nokers(Mongolian Soldiers)..

1071
01:50:45,566 --> 01:50:47,365
We are stronger.

1072
01:50:48,846 --> 01:50:52,565
It is in your best interest to
trust what this Hatun says.

1073
01:50:53,126 --> 01:50:56,245
For Osman Bey's insight is worth a thousand men.

1074
01:51:02,446 --> 01:51:07,205
You said he was your
Hatun's brother and let him in.

1075
01:51:07,606 --> 01:51:08,845
Ilbay...

1076
01:51:09,126 --> 01:51:10,245
Do you...

1077
01:51:10,806 --> 01:51:12,485
..trust him

1078
01:51:19,366 --> 01:51:21,445
I trust Yusuf Bey.

1079
01:51:22,446 --> 01:51:25,245
My brother pledged...

1080
01:51:25,246 --> 01:51:27,605
...allegiance to Ilbay Bey.

1081
01:51:28,086 --> 01:51:30,405
There is no need to discuss it, Ulugan.

1082
01:51:30,686 --> 01:51:32,565
Weren't you the ones...

1083
01:51:32,966 --> 01:51:36,005
...who pledged allegiance to Osman?

1084
01:51:37,126 --> 01:51:39,245
Trust doesn't fall from the sky.

1085
01:51:39,606 --> 01:51:41,045
It is gained.

1086
01:51:41,566 --> 01:51:44,245
Your brother will prove himself.

1087
01:51:48,086 --> 01:51:49,405
Nokers(Mongolian Soldiers)!

1088
01:51:49,526 --> 01:51:51,685
Bring the other Bey's son here!

1089
01:52:00,926 --> 01:52:02,485
You're exhausted Osman.

1090
01:52:02,806 --> 01:52:05,965
-You can't hold anymore.
-I will never seek mercy!

1091
01:52:06,206 --> 01:52:08,365
I will fight to the last drop of my blood.

1092
01:52:08,806 --> 01:52:13,085
-Come to me, dogs.
-Nokers(Mongolian Soldiers), you all attack!

1093
01:52:22,006 --> 01:52:24,125
Come to me.

1094
01:52:25,726 --> 01:52:26,965
Run away, girl.

1095
01:52:27,126 --> 01:52:28,845
You're not alone, huh?

1096
01:52:29,086 --> 01:52:31,205
Catch her and kill

1097
01:52:43,006 --> 01:52:44,805
We're here, Osman!

1098
01:52:46,846 --> 01:52:49,765
-Bala?
-We're here.

1099
01:52:50,366 --> 01:52:52,245
Attack!

1100
01:53:00,926 --> 01:53:03,805
-Cerkutay.
Say no more words.

1101
01:53:04,566 --> 01:53:07,885
No words to say. Only swords will speak now.

1102
01:53:07,966 --> 01:53:09,765
Here we go.

1103
01:53:16,566 --> 01:53:18,685
You dogs!

1104
01:53:18,766 --> 01:53:23,605
You took him captive but he's never alone!

1105
01:53:33,726 --> 01:53:35,285
I will make Ghazi a noker(Mongolian Soldier).

1106
01:53:35,326 --> 01:53:37,285
His life will belong to us.

1107
01:53:37,366 --> 01:53:42,085
-He won't be a rat like you.
-You think I'll leave my son to you?

1108
01:53:42,566 --> 01:53:47,685
I won't show mercy anymore
just because you are my brother.

1109
01:54:09,486 --> 01:54:11,045
My Bey!

1110
01:54:26,766 --> 01:54:29,445
Alps, Cerkutay.

1111
01:54:32,126 --> 01:54:34,445
May Allah give you a long life, my Bey.

1112
01:54:34,606 --> 01:54:37,645
Are you alright, my Bey?
We can provide what we lost.

1113
01:54:37,926 --> 01:54:40,645
If you live, the state will live.

1114
01:54:41,606 --> 01:54:42,885
Osman.

1115
01:54:43,246 --> 01:54:44,925
Are you alright?
-I'm good.

1116
01:54:46,886 --> 01:54:48,365
Are you good?

1117
01:54:48,486 --> 01:54:51,925
-How are you?
-Good. What did you do on your own?

1118
01:54:52,006 --> 01:54:55,245
Don't worry. I wasn't on my
own. Meryem was with me.

1119
01:54:57,806 --> 01:55:00,685
Meryem, what are you doing here?

1120
01:55:00,846 --> 01:55:02,805
You're wounded.

1121
01:55:03,686 --> 01:55:06,365
It's fine. Not a big deal.

1122
01:55:07,086 --> 01:55:10,325
I didn't want to just wait in the tribe.

1123
01:55:11,006 --> 01:55:14,005
I tracked them to help Osman Bey.

1124
01:55:15,446 --> 01:55:20,165
I was going to save his life
but he saved my life instead.

1125
01:55:20,726 --> 01:55:23,125
Praise be, my girl.

1126
01:55:23,686 --> 01:55:27,885
We don't know your parents but
obviously you have noble blood.

1127
01:55:29,326 --> 01:55:33,445
My Osman is alright. You are alright as well.

1128
01:55:33,766 --> 01:55:38,765
Even this dark night is enlightened for me.
-Well, Bala...

1129
01:55:39,486 --> 01:55:42,413
If your motherly attitude
is enough, we should go.

1130
01:55:42,425 --> 01:55:43,405
Osman.

1131
01:55:43,606 --> 01:55:44,845
Bala.

1132
01:55:45,446 --> 01:55:47,365
You never know what Altuga will do.

1133
01:55:47,566 --> 01:55:50,045
He's going to gather his men. We need to go.

1134
01:55:50,526 --> 01:55:53,565
Alright. But we need to let Orhan know first.

1135
01:55:53,606 --> 01:55:56,005
-They're near Sarical.
-Alright.

1136
01:55:56,246 --> 01:55:57,365
-Aykurt.
-My Bey.

1137
01:55:57,446 --> 01:56:00,245
Inform them quickly. We're going to the south.

1138
01:56:00,486 --> 01:56:03,645
We have a duty to perform and a battle to fight.

1139
01:56:03,686 --> 01:56:06,365
-Let's go.
As you order, my Bey.

1140
01:56:08,646 --> 01:56:10,765
Come on.

1141
01:56:15,166 --> 01:56:17,565
Get off! Get off!

1142
01:56:18,646 --> 01:56:19,965
Get off!

1143
01:56:22,366 --> 01:56:24,245
Why did you bring me here?

1144
01:56:24,486 --> 01:56:26,405
What do you want, dastards?

1145
01:56:31,206 --> 01:56:35,405
Yusuf, just like your treacherous sister...

1146
01:56:35,646 --> 01:56:38,725
...are you attempting treason?

1147
01:56:40,566 --> 01:56:43,085
Speak. What are you doing here?

1148
01:56:44,006 --> 01:56:45,245
Speak!

1149
01:57:03,646 --> 01:57:08,045
You are loyal to Osman Bey, huh?

1150
01:57:08,526 --> 01:57:11,405
For sure, you dog.

1151
01:57:12,846 --> 01:57:18,765
I'm loyal to Osman Bey, my
Shahzades and my state...

1152
01:57:18,886 --> 01:57:21,005
..to the end.

1153
01:57:42,046 --> 01:57:44,245
It's your turn, Yusuf.

1154
01:57:47,846 --> 01:57:50,205
Show me whose you are loyal to.

1155
01:57:54,886 --> 01:57:56,725
What a coincidence.

1156
01:57:59,446 --> 01:58:01,645
I wish I would kill you too.

1157
01:58:03,846 --> 01:58:05,365
Like your father Bayhan.

1158
01:58:07,646 --> 01:58:11,885
Don't mention my martyr father's
name with your filthy mouth again!

1159
01:58:13,806 --> 01:58:15,605
Come on.

1160
01:58:15,726 --> 01:58:17,245
Grab the dagger.

1161
01:58:17,526 --> 01:58:19,805
Do what the dog said, Yusuf!

1162
01:58:19,846 --> 01:58:24,165
If you don't, I swear...

1163
01:58:24,406 --> 01:58:28,125
..I will do the same to you.

1164
01:58:29,446 --> 01:58:30,725
Come on!

1165
01:58:30,966 --> 01:58:32,925
This took too long.

1166
01:58:37,566 --> 01:58:39,165
Take the dagger.

1167
01:58:41,246 --> 01:58:42,445
Come on.

1168
01:58:53,726 --> 01:58:55,965
-Come on!
-Yusuf.

1169
01:58:56,566 --> 01:58:58,085
Come on, brother.

1170
01:58:58,526 --> 01:58:59,925
Do it.

1171
01:59:08,166 --> 01:59:09,845
Come on!

1172
01:59:10,686 --> 01:59:14,045
You coward!

1173
01:59:33,366 --> 01:59:35,325
Good.

1174
01:59:59,246 --> 02:00:04,045
Commander Ulugan, Osman escaped.

1175
02:00:14,886 --> 02:00:16,845
He escaped?

1176
02:00:22,326 --> 02:00:25,605
I told you not to underestimate Osman!

1177
02:00:25,966 --> 02:00:27,765
We found his trails, commander.

1178
02:00:28,246 --> 02:00:31,285
Altuga must have captured him by now.

1179
02:00:32,766 --> 02:00:34,645
Lead the way.

1180
02:00:35,206 --> 02:00:38,205
Take me to him. Lead the way!

1181
02:00:55,166 --> 02:00:57,365
We've been riding since last night, my Bey.

1182
02:00:57,486 --> 02:01:00,765
-Our sons catch up soon, God willing.
-Don't worry, Bala.

1183
02:01:01,046 --> 02:01:04,525
-We'll get out of this trouble all together.
-Of course we will.

1184
02:01:04,646 --> 02:01:07,045
But I can't just swallow this, my Bey.

1185
02:01:07,086 --> 02:01:09,685
I was expecting Begum to do such a thing, but...

1186
02:01:09,726 --> 02:01:12,605
...what Ilbay did hurt me a lot.

1187
02:01:12,846 --> 02:01:15,045
We're being tested with our own kin.

1188
02:01:15,046 --> 02:01:17,445
Our destination is Ilah-i Kalimatullah.

1189
02:01:17,486 --> 02:01:20,285
So we won't show mercy
whoever stands against us.

1190
02:01:29,006 --> 02:01:33,045
My Bey, Ulugan and his nokers
(Mongolian Soldiers) are coming towards here.

1191
02:01:33,126 --> 02:01:34,805
They found our tracks.

1192
02:01:35,926 --> 02:01:38,925
Then we will make them
lose our tracks. Let's go!

1193
02:01:56,686 --> 02:01:58,205
Where is Osman?

1194
02:01:59,926 --> 02:02:02,325
I followed them all night. Commander Ulugan.

1195
02:02:02,566 --> 02:02:05,445
They've gone that way. We should hurry.

1196
02:02:06,166 --> 02:02:08,765
If you show such weakness again

1197
02:02:09,086 --> 02:02:11,125
...I will cut off
your head, Altuga.

1198
02:02:16,006 --> 02:02:17,965
Let's hunt the wolf.

1199
02:02:37,926 --> 02:02:40,365
They're going towards the south.

1200
02:02:41,046 --> 02:02:44,325
But nokers (Mongolian Soldiers)
must be looking for them too.

1201
02:02:44,606 --> 02:02:46,645
We should be careful.

1202
02:02:50,366 --> 02:02:52,245
Holofira.

1203
02:02:53,726 --> 02:02:54,925
Holofira.

1204
02:02:55,166 --> 02:02:57,285
-Are you alright?
-I'm fine.

1205
02:02:57,686 --> 02:03:00,965
-It's nothing. Don't worry.
-My Holofira.

1206
02:03:01,566 --> 02:03:03,605
You say you're fine...

1207
02:03:03,966 --> 02:03:05,645
...but your eyes look pale.

1208
02:03:05,846 --> 02:03:07,605
Don't be stubborn.

1209
02:03:07,806 --> 02:03:10,205
Go to Ulgen Hatun and have some rest.

1210
02:03:11,206 --> 02:03:12,325
No, Orhan.

1211
02:03:12,446 --> 02:03:17,365
If I don't stand beside you now, the
bed I'm lying on will swallow me like mud.

1212
02:03:17,686 --> 02:03:19,525
Your presence gives me strength.

1213
02:03:19,686 --> 02:03:21,885
We will go meet Osman Bey together.

1214
02:03:22,126 --> 02:03:25,165
-Tell her something. Alaaddin.
-Holofira is strong, brother.

1215
02:03:25,366 --> 02:03:27,605
It's better she stays with you...

1216
02:03:27,646 --> 02:03:32,045
...instead of going reluctantly
and worrying about you.

1217
02:03:32,046 --> 02:03:34,285
-Alaaddin.
-Orhan Bey.

1218
02:03:34,406 --> 02:03:36,525
I told you on the way.

1219
02:03:36,886 --> 02:03:39,925
I will look after Holofira's two lives.

1220
02:03:42,326 --> 02:03:44,325
Don't be worrying, brother.

1221
02:03:44,846 --> 02:03:46,725
Fine. Fine.

1222
02:03:47,646 --> 02:03:48,885
Let's go.

1223
02:03:49,086 --> 02:03:50,765
You go first, hatuns.

1224
02:03:50,966 --> 02:03:53,245
Come on, come on.

1225
02:04:15,566 --> 02:04:17,325
You traitors.

1226
02:04:22,646 --> 02:04:24,285
Wherever you

1227
02:04:24,366 --> 02:04:26,205
...you can't run away from me, Osman.

1228
02:04:40,046 --> 02:04:41,925
Not this time, Osman.

1229
02:04:44,566 --> 02:04:46,805
You can't run off this time.

1230
02:04:48,726 --> 02:04:50,365
They've surrounded us.

1231
02:04:50,566 --> 02:04:52,525
This is it, Bala!

1232
02:04:53,246 --> 02:04:56,485
Nobody can save you from me now!

1233
02:04:57,206 --> 02:04:58,885
You say so?

1234
02:05:00,526 --> 02:05:02,805
I will come back for all of you.

1235
02:05:03,806 --> 02:05:06,365
Then you will beg me

1236
02:05:08,486 --> 02:05:10,965
But I will show no mercy..

1237
02:05:13,126 --> 02:05:15,325
..for any of you.

1238
02:05:17,926 --> 02:05:19,565
We're drawing back.

1239
02:05:26,806 --> 02:05:28,565
Go wherever you want.

1240
02:05:29,006 --> 02:05:33,325
Where you will end up in
the end is Olcaytu Khan's feet.

1241
02:05:35,006 --> 02:05:38,485
Red Woman, you stay here with me.

1242
02:05:39,006 --> 02:05:42,245
We never know what evil
things Lukas and you can do.

1243
02:05:42,446 --> 02:05:44,205
Let's go!

1244
02:06:03,286 --> 02:06:06,565
We can't ride on. We have to go on foot.

1245
02:06:12,406 --> 02:06:15,365
Meryem, Bala. You go first.

1246
02:06:41,846 --> 02:06:44,645
This is the end, Osman.

1247
02:06:48,006 --> 02:06:49,765
We're trapped.

1248
02:06:53,686 --> 02:06:57,125
My Bey, we clear the way. You should just go.

1249
02:06:58,366 --> 02:07:00,365
Stay behind me.

1250
02:07:01,046 --> 02:07:03,805
I will kill you before Ulugan arrives.

1251
02:07:25,766 --> 02:07:28,725
Someone's coming. Take your positions.

1252
02:08:01,366 --> 02:08:03,045
Look, look.

1253
02:08:03,526 --> 02:08:08,005
While I was looking for the
father, Tengri offered me his baby!

1254
02:08:09,006 --> 02:08:10,685
What you're chasing...

1255
02:08:11,206 --> 02:08:13,765
...is only your death, vile dog.

1256
02:08:27,926 --> 02:08:29,365
Ilbay.

1257
02:08:31,046 --> 02:08:32,845
Begum Hatun.

1258
02:08:34,766 --> 02:08:37,645
-You...
-Yes!

1259
02:08:38,206 --> 02:08:41,765
-Call us the new masters of Kayi!
-What are you talking about?

1260
02:08:44,366 --> 02:08:49,565
You joined us to wait for
the day when you'd bite, huh?

1261
02:08:52,326 --> 02:08:55,565
I swear you'll pay for your treason!

1262
02:08:56,846 --> 02:08:58,965
Listen to me carefully, Ulugan.

1263
02:08:59,326 --> 02:09:01,765
You and those dastards with you...

1264
02:09:02,086 --> 02:09:05,205
...you will all die by our swords.

1265
02:09:05,886 --> 02:09:09,525
The sword of justice of Osman
Bey who you tried to kill...

1266
02:09:10,246 --> 02:09:11,565
...will...

1267
02:09:12,806 --> 02:09:15,365
...surely cut your head off.

1268
02:09:15,686 --> 02:09:18,645
Don't worry, Osman's dog.

1269
02:09:19,286 --> 02:09:23,125
Until Olcaytu Khan wants Osman to die...

1270
02:09:23,126 --> 02:09:25,685
...he will live in my chains.

1271
02:09:29,606 --> 02:09:33,405
But death is the only way for you.

1272
02:09:34,686 --> 02:09:39,565
If we die, we'll become martyrs, if you
die, you'll just become corpses, you dog!

1273
02:09:42,086 --> 02:09:43,205
Come on!

1274
02:09:43,726 --> 02:09:45,765
Draw your sword!

1275
02:09:50,606 --> 02:09:53,525
Orhan, there are too many of them.

1276
02:10:03,926 --> 02:10:07,445
I will kill you with my own sword!

1277
02:10:09,326 --> 02:10:11,725
Now your era is over!

1278
02:10:11,886 --> 02:10:17,005
I will burn and destroy your lands and borders!

1279
02:10:17,206 --> 02:10:18,845
Know this..

1280
02:10:19,166 --> 02:10:22,725
Only my sword determines
the borders on these lands.

1281
02:10:24,526 --> 02:10:29,045
Do you have the courage, huh? Do you? Face me!

1282
02:10:29,046 --> 02:10:33,085
It's been a long time since I
ripped your heart out, Osman.

1283
02:10:33,926 --> 02:10:36,045
We hurt you in such a way that...

1284
02:10:36,446 --> 02:10:38,245
...you didn't even notice it.

1285
02:10:39,606 --> 02:10:40,885
Your grandchild.

1286
02:10:43,046 --> 02:10:45,085
Alaeddin's baby...

1287
02:10:45,966 --> 02:10:48,445
I killed it in Gonca's womb.

1288
02:10:48,566 --> 02:10:51,485
What?

1289
02:10:59,286 --> 02:11:01,205
Did you kill my grandchild?

1290
02:11:05,766 --> 02:11:08,085
Did you kill

1291
02:11:08,966 --> 02:11:10,765
Did you kill?

1292
02:11:12,686 --> 02:11:14,445
I swear..

1293
02:11:15,166 --> 02:11:17,045
I swear.

1294
02:11:17,686 --> 02:11:20,845
I swear on this world...

1295
02:11:21,086 --> 02:11:22,485
...while you die...

1296
02:11:22,766 --> 02:11:24,925
...you will ask for my forgiveness.

1297
02:11:25,046 --> 02:11:27,885
You will beg me, you dog!

1298
02:11:27,886 --> 02:11:31,765
You will answer me today!

1299
02:11:31,886 --> 02:11:33,645
I will kill you all.

1300
02:11:34,926 --> 02:11:37,205
This land is my land!

1301
02:11:38,166 --> 02:11:43,685
If we're not destined to walk on it,
we know how to lie under it as well.

1302
02:11:43,686 --> 02:11:49,005
If your preaching is over, I will be
finishing the short epic you wrote, Osman.

1303
02:11:49,006 --> 02:11:50,965
No, you are wrong.

1304
02:11:52,406 --> 02:11:55,005
My epic is just beginning.

1305
02:11:55,006 --> 02:11:57,365
Come, you dog!

1306
02:12:28,326 --> 02:12:31,045
Now you have no breath to take.

1307
02:12:31,046 --> 02:12:34,605
You ruled with blood, and you
will pay the price with your life.

1308
02:12:34,606 --> 02:12:36,205
Not this time, Osman!

1309
02:12:36,206 --> 02:12:39,605
You will pay the price this time.

1310
02:12:47,686 --> 02:12:53,085
Soldiers! Kill Bala and the girl!

1311
02:13:00,806 --> 02:13:06,405
Meryem

1312
02:13:08,886 --> 02:13:12,085
Meryem!

1313
02:13:14,966 --> 02:13:19,885
Meryem! Hold my hand! Give me your hand, Meryem!

1314
02:13:19,886 --> 02:13:23,005
Bala!

1315
02:13:24,846 --> 02:13:28,125
Bala!

1316
02:13:28,126 --> 02:13:30,325
Hold my hand, my daughter!

1317
02:13:30,686 --> 02:13:33,805
Osman!

1318
02:13:34,006 --> 02:13:36,525
Come on! Go!

1319
02:13:36,886 --> 02:13:40,045
Your Hatun is calling you! You cannot go...

1320
02:13:40,046 --> 02:13:43,205
Because you are all alone, Osman

1321
02:13:43,206 --> 02:13:45,285
You are all alone!

1322
02:13:46,406 --> 02:13:49,845
I am not strong enough,
Bala Hatun. I cannot do it...

1323
02:13:49,846 --> 02:13:53,645
Hold me... Here. I got it.
-I cannot...

1324
02:13:54,566 --> 02:13:57,445
I will not let you go. I will not.

1325
02:13:57,446 --> 02:13:58,534
Please, don't...

1326
02:13:58,546 --> 02:14:01,845
Alright, my daughter.I
am here. It will be alright.

1327
02:14:02,966 --> 02:14:05,205
Meryem, don't look down! Look at me!

1328
02:14:05,206 --> 02:14:08,405
Bala Hatun, I am too tired!

1329
02:14:09,446 --> 02:14:10,525
Osman.

1330
02:14:13,526 --> 02:14:15,085
Where are you going Osman?

1331
02:14:15,086 --> 02:14:17,125
You were going to make me pay the price!

1332
02:14:17,126 --> 02:14:18,565
Your era is over!

1333
02:14:18,566 --> 02:14:20,565
Now we will rule!

1334
02:14:20,566 --> 02:14:22,765
Even if everyone turns into a jackal...

1335
02:14:22,766 --> 02:14:24,885
...I will always be the lone wolf.

1336
02:14:25,406 --> 02:14:29,685
I never knelt before someone! And
I will never kneel before someone!

1337
02:14:32,886 --> 02:14:38,045
Meryem no! No, Meryem! Come on Meryem!

1338
02:14:39,646 --> 02:14:41,485
Come on, Osman!